{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone","id":704348,"title":"It's possible to coerce a vampire to Embrace someone?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-16T22:55:16-07:00","id":704348,"title":"It's possible to coerce a vampire to Embrace someone?","content":"If a vampire is caged and chained, and threatened with torture ( both starvation and fire ), it's possible to coerce him to embrace someone?<br /> <br /> If that is possible, could a fugitive / independent ghoul that managed to imprison a vampire force him to &quot;produce&quot; new vampires for him ( he kidnap humans, chain them, bring them to the chained vampire, force him to embrace them, then he feed them with pig or cow blood bought at the local slaughterhouse, then he drains them of vitae when needed ) in order to have a vaste supply of Vitae and not incur in Vinculum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T23:17:46-07:00","id":704376,"title":"","content":"It's possible, I suppose. Depends on the personality of the vampire. But if you're just handing them live humans, it's also very risky. Every drop of blood they swallow refuels their power and they have sooooo many ways they can break free of whatever restraints you put them in. Generally, however, embracing somebody takes a toll on the vampire's mind and / or soul. Forcing a vampire to mass embrace means they aren't going to be useful to you for very long before they devolve into a Revenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T23:22:43-07:00","id":704378,"title":"","content":"Why wouldn't it incur Vinculum? I guess you could keep it at low levels if you only drink from each vampire once. If nothing else, you could try to force Hunger frenzies and hope for Revenants. I'm not sure if Revenant blood works for Ghouls or not.<br /> <br /> Either way, it might work for a while depending on the vampire, but you'll end up with a Draugr whose Beast starts developing Vigor very quickly. Fun times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T23:27:07-07:00","id":704414,"title":"","content":"I mean...yeah? You might have an argument on whether or not someone can directly mind control you into doing it (and that probably relies on how that mind control interacts with Breaking Points, but I digress), but if you're asking if someone can force a vampire to choose between embracing someone or death (or pain or whatever) then yes, it's absolutely possible. Couple of notes for this specific plan:<br /> <br /> - If you stick with a single &quot;mother&quot; vampire doing all the Embracing, then the Humanity cost will eventually drive him or her to be an unreasoning monster that you -can't- really bargain with. (Also, I'm unsure if Draugr can Embrace intentionally given their lack of Humanity. Hm.)<br /> <br /> - Animal blood is super inefficient, so depending on the needs of the ghoul(s) it can end up causing a noticeable drain. Or it won't! A lot depends on the smarts of the ghoul and what preparations he or she has made. There's probably going to be some sort of paper trail or anomalies that can lead back to her (if only for drama's sake).<br /> <br /> - Sticking with one childer for your blood harvest still puts you in danger of vinculum, and this plan does nothing about Blood Addiction. You can circumvent the first point by disposing of a certain childer after two drinks (if the vinculum will let you at that point, hm.) and cycle in a new one, but that leads directly into...<br /> <br /> - Any ghoul who does this is a <i>fucking psychopath</i> and their Integrity is not long for this world, since this entire plans is an unending cycle of torture and death. I really hope this isn't a PC plan, for your sake.<br /> <br /> - You could probably change the plan somewhat to change up exactly how it plays out: you could start small but use each given childer to create more vampires and turn it into a blood farm, and it's probably more efficient to find a way to supplement your animal blood use with kidnapped human vessels, if only because you're going to be kidnapping more people -anyways- to make more vampires and humans will feed more of these livestock Kindred efficiently. You might also want to invest in multiple locations and even find ways to monetize it, for surely at this level you're going to need conspirators to make it work. Note: this makes the plan way more noticeable and nothing about making the process cleaner and more efficient makes it <i>any less fucking crazy.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 10-17-2015, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T23:38:11-07:00","id":704421,"title":"","content":"Honestly, you could make this plan work, but it would be so much practical trouble to go to to keep everything working, between all the lossy blood collection for Vitae, repeated kidnappings, managing both intelligent vampires and draugr, juggling blood sources to keep yourself topped up without invoking a blood bond, that the ghoul might as well just skip the middleman, take the Curse on the chin and get a vampire to Embrace him instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T23:42:44-07:00","id":704424,"title":"","content":"And now I'm refining this idea as a Kindred plot to keep elders and trusted ghouls fed by turning prisoners lined up for execution into seed for a blood farm, where they're drained, forced to Embrace, then eventually staked and drained dry. I feel like a horrible person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 10-17-2015, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T00:10:52-07:00","id":704434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=704424#post704424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now I'm refining this idea as a Kindred plot to keep elders and trusted ghouls fed by turning prisoners lined up for execution into seed for a blood farm, where they're drained, forced to Embrace, then eventually staked and drained dry. I feel like a horrible person.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wow. I am so stealing this. I wonder how many holding cells are needed for this kind of operation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Improper use of inverted commas, Hoover!&quot; - Herr Starr","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8536-nutshell","name":"Nutshell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T06:08:35-07:00","id":704744,"title":"","content":"You'd likely need a supply of animals, too. To feed the post-Embraced vampires, to get their Vitae levels up for proper &quot;transference&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course, any Neonate or Ancillae that get's word of this and spreads it would bring a firestorm down on the elders doing this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T08:12:29-07:00","id":705105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone#post704348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a vampire is caged and chained, and threatened with torture ( both starvation and fire ), it's possible to coerce him to embrace someone?<br /> <br /> If that is possible, could a fugitive / independent ghoul that managed to imprison a vampire force him to &quot;produce&quot; new vampires for him ( he kidnap humans, chain them, bring them to the chained vampire, force him to embrace them, then he feed them with pig or cow blood bought at the local slaughterhouse, then he drains them of vitae when needed ) in order to have a vaste supply of Vitae and not incur in Vinculum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can a Vampire coerced into doing it doesn't want to yes.<br /> By a ghoul maybe maybe not.<br /> While second edition ghouls have more agency statwise they don't do well against vamps and automatically fail powers of blood against a regnent.<br /> Look at feeding from animal rules you don't get a lot vitae out of their blood not even large animals.<br /> And the hell would a starving kindred have enough vitae to sire.<br /> <br /> And remember every clan has access to commanding beast aspect or the seductive aspect.<br /> I don't see how the ghoul won't let the kindred go given time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T09:50:21-07:00","id":705253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone#post704348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a vampire is caged and chained, and threatened with torture ( both starvation and fire ), it's possible to coerce him to embrace someone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always wanted to run a character who stole the Embrace- even just the roleplaying potential in &quot;holy crap, a human <i>gatecrashed</i> us. Do we just, like, kill him, because that <i>was</i> pretty impressive&quot; sounds like fun. The process of coercion sounds pretty similar for both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T10:10:21-07:00","id":705331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=704414#post704414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean...yeah? You might have an argument on whether or not someone can directly mind control you into doing it (and that probably relies on how that mind control interacts with Breaking Points, but I digress), but if you're asking if someone can force a vampire to choose between embracing someone or death (or pain or whatever) then yes, it's absolutely possible. Couple of notes for this specific plan:<br /> <br /> - If you stick with a single &quot;mother&quot; vampire doing all the Embracing, then the Humanity cost will eventually drive him or her to be an unreasoning monster that you -can't- really bargain with. (Also, I'm unsure if Draugr can Embrace intentionally given their lack of Humanity. Hm.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Most probably can, though chances of the childe being another Draugr or a Larva from Wicked Dead should be considerable. even one who does come out as kindred might be &quot;mentally tainted&quot; in some way, depending on how a ST runs it.<br /> <br /> In case you're asking yourself about my sources, i'm mostly extrapolating from a sample PC in Gangrel: Savage &amp; Macabre who happens to be a Draugr-childe and had a &quot;fight and flight for its unlife&quot; moment right out of embrace...so, sort of canon(ish) in a fluffy way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T11:17:17-07:00","id":705490,"title":"","content":"Err....<br /> I'm sorry, I guess I had to state that from the beginning.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about the FIRST EDITION of the New World of Darkness. In the first edition any Vampire with Blood Potency inferior to 3 ( aka: less than 100 years ) can feed on animal blood without any real problem, it just need 2 liters for 1 vita. Now, animal blood bought from slaughterhouses cost 3.5 dollars / liter, so feeding a prisoner fledgling vampire requires just 200 dollars for month.<br /> <br /> Also, first edition vampires expend Willpower dots, not Humanity. So they become spineless Willpower 0 vampires, not draugr.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=704376#post704376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible, I suppose. Depends on the personality of the vampire. But if you're just handing them live humans, it's also very risky. Every drop of blood they swallow refuels their power and they have sooooo many ways they can break free of whatever restraints you put them in. Generally, however, embracing somebody takes a toll on the vampire's mind and / or soul. Forcing a vampire to mass embrace means they aren't going to be useful to you for very long before they devolve into a Revenant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To develop Vinculum it's necessary to drink three times. You can drink two times from that vampire, force him to embrace two or three kidnapped humans, kill him, then do the same with the newborn vampires.<br /> <br /> Also, these nurtured vampire would be quite easy to control. They would have only basic istinctive knowledge of their clan disciplines and no hint on how to develope new powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Either way, it might work for a while depending on the vampire, but you'll end up with a Draugr whose Beast starts developing Vigor very quickly. Fun times </div> </div> </div>It's not necessary to bring the vampire to Draugr state. After he embraced a new vampire, it becomes disposable. The new vampire then can embrace some others and be disposed too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You'd likely need a supply of animals, too. To feed the post-Embraced vampires, to get their Vitae levels up for proper &quot;transference&quot; </div> </div> </div>That's quite easy, slaughterhouses legally sells pig and cow blood for alimentary purposes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And remember every clan has access to commanding beast aspect or the seductive aspect.<br /> I don't see how the ghoul won't let the kindred go given time. </div> </div> </div>If a vampire is bond by thick steel chains, has an helmet that stops him from making eye-contact and a jaw locker that prevents him to speak, he can't use any kind of Domination or Majesty power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-17-2015, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T12:10:58-07:00","id":705604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=705490#post705490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err....<br /> To develop Vinculum it's necessary to drink three times. You can drink two times from that vampire, force him to embrace two or three kidnapped humans, kill him, then do the same with the newborn vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Vinculum isn't a binary state. Each drink produces a progressive effect. It takes three drinks before it becomes so long-lasting and all-consuming, but you only get a single donation of Vitae from each entire vampire if you want to avoid feeling any affection for your captives beyond thinking they are delicious. That's a lot of kidnapped humans and carefully bound vampires for not much Vitae return.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I think the main problem with this plan isn't imprisoning the vampires and managing the blood bond, it's all the attention you're going to attract from kidnapping so many humans and obtaining such obscene quantities of animal blood. It's a great idea if you want a serial killer manhunt out for you eventually. Stealing the Embrace and being a vampire yourself is much more blood-efficient, and so allows you to feed far less conspicuously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T12:43:26-07:00","id":705635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=705490#post705490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err....<br /> <br /> <br /> If a vampire is bond by thick steel chains, has an helmet that stops him from making eye-contact and a jaw locker that prevents him to speak, he can't use any kind of Domination or Majesty power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gonna disagree, he can sit / stand / lay there in his restraints, looking seductive as fuck while the Ghoul begins tearing their clothes off.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then there's the fact vampires can regenerate from anything that doesn't outright slay them. Gnawing your appendages off isn't quite as big a desperation move as it sounds when you'll have your arm back within a week.<br /> <br /> Vampires trained in Protean can also...<br /> <br /> A) Grow claws and rip their way out of their confinement.<br /> <br /> B) Merge with the walls / floors / ceiling to deprive you of your vampire farm.<br /> <br /> C) <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Turn into animals and slip through places humans can't.<br /> <br /> D) Turn into mist and poof out of the room.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> C and D might be overcome with an air tight prison, but if they use B, your only option is to carve them out of the scenery, which sounds like a lot of time and effort. Option A is likely to get you killed by a very pissed off vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T13:23:54-07:00","id":705651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Frankly, I think the main problem with this plan isn't imprisoning the vampires and managing the blood bond, it's all the attention you're going to attract from kidnapping so many humans and obtaining such obscene quantities of animal blood. </div> </div> </div>I don't know how it works in second edition. In first edition NWod, a Ghoul requires 1 monthly point of Vitae to stay a Ghoul. Assuming he has decent constitution ( 3 ) and drink from every vampire once, he needs to kidnap one human every 3 months. It's way less collateral damage than the average vampire does.<br /> <br /> About the animal blood, it's 60 lts / months. Slaughterhouses routinely throws gallons of blood every months and manage to sell just a small part of it. Also, with a bit of resources, having a few pigs and/or cows and taking small quantities of blood from them would do the job.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gonna disagree, he can sit / stand / lay there in his restraints, looking seductive as fuck while the Ghoul begins tearing their clothes off. </div> </div> </div>Majesty isn't mind control, it can't force a subject to do a blatantly suicidal action ( like unrestrain the vampire ). That would require Domination ( that requires hearing an eye contact ). Also, it's possible to reflexively spend Willpower to resist Majesty and there are heavy bonuses if the vampire is an enemy (+1 ) and if it poses a deadly threat (+2 ). The Ghould could keep a remote control at hand and non-lethally ( but painfully ) elettrocute the vampire at the first hint he's using tricks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then there's the fact vampires can regenerate from anything that doesn't outright slay them. Gnawing your appendages off isn't quite as big a desperation move as it sounds when you'll have your arm back within a week. </div> </div> </div>To reach an arm you would need to move more-or-less the jaws. With a jaw locker and head bound by chains there's literally no way to do that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A) Grow claws and rip their way out of their confinement.<br /> <br /> B) Merge with the walls / floors / ceiling to deprive you of your vampire farm.<br /> <br /> C) <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Turn into animals and slip through places humans can't.<br /> <br /> D) Turn into mist and poof out of the room.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Claw through steel? To do that, even moving freely, I would require at least Strenght 7-8 or several dots in Vigor. But a vampire with vrists and arms bound by steel chains can't move his claws enough to reach the chains and cut them. He would have to break the chains with brute force, that would be possible for an elder, mabye.<br /> <br /> Other options ( protean powers ) would seriously put in danger the warden, but they're advanced powers. I was thinking about abducting a young, relatively powerless vampire.<br /> Clearly, anything stronger than a Neonate would be able to escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-17-2015, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T13:35:02-07:00","id":705678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=705651#post705651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know how it works in second edition. In first edition NWod, a Ghoul requires 1 monthly point of Vitae to stay a Ghoul. Assuming he has decent constitution ( 3 ) and drink from every vampire once, he needs to kidnap one human every 3 months. It's way less collateral damage than the average vampire does.</div> </div> </div> </div>That assumes this ghoul, who has a vampire captive in his basement he regularly has to coerce, and who keeps overpowering humans every few months, isn't burning his Vitae on anything else. And even given that, one human disappears every three months? Yeah, I think that's going to be noticed sooner or later. One or two disappearances in an area can be covered up. A minimum of four in a year is starting to play with fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T13:45:28-07:00","id":705682,"title":"","content":"A ghoul who hunts vampires for vitae is not necessarily a bad idea, but this implementation requires way too many &quot;what ifs&quot; to really work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T13:47:39-07:00","id":705683,"title":"","content":"There's a few rogue ghouls that exist in the setting, most notably the founder of the Malleus Maleficarum. Mythologies has a number of 'ghouls' who are immune to the vinculum, or at least highly resistant. While most people look upon ghouls as simple slaves, its actually a concept fraught with danger for the regnant.<br /> <br /> Regarding vampires being coerced to Embrace, sure it can happen. There's a couple bloodlines known for having blood that cannot inflict a blood bond, and it wouldn't be hard to imagine a powerful vampire catching one and manipulating it into Embracing so that it may have a number of reliable sources for Vitae.<br /> <br /> In both of these situations, however, remember that characters in the World of Darkness do not have access to the Vampire the Requiem corebook and the character sheets of all the vampires in town so they know exactly how to work things out to counter all their abilities. For every vampire that knows of the bloodline that doesn't inflict a blood bond, there's likely a dozen that haven't even heard of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-17-2015, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T14:54:47-07:00","id":705745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=705678#post705678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That assumes this ghoul, who has a vampire captive in his basement he regularly has to coerce, and who keeps overpowering humans every few months, isn't burning his Vitae on anything else. And even given that, one human disappears every three months? Yeah, I think that's going to be noticed sooner or later. One or two disappearances in an area can be covered up. A minimum of four in a year is starting to play with fire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, not necessarely every time the same one. He could:<br /> <br /> 1- capture his first vampire ( that's the most tricky part )<br /> 2- kidnap a human and coerce the first vampire into embracing him<br /> 3- takes the blood from the first vampire<br /> 4- kill the first vampire ( or put a stick in his heart and save him for future experiments )<br /> 5- Kidnap another human and coerce the second vampire ( a confused, scared weakling with no true grasp on his powers ) into embracing him<br /> 6- take the blood from the second vampire<br /> 7- kill or put a stick into the second vampire<br /> <br /> and so on. Coercing with fire and starvation a neonate that knows nothing about vampirism should be quite easy.<br /> <br /> About kidnapping humans, if he have a car, a basement in the desert ( or in a barren plain, or in the midst of a forest ) he can take a ride, drive some hours, and kidnap junkies, hookers and bums from different areas for minimum heat. A Ghoul has not the problem of daylight nor the need to feed on a daily basis. Mabye I'm getting it wrong but, from what I read, most vampires kills way more than 4 humans in a year.<br /> <br /> Also, if he have even a single dot of Majesty, Domination or Obscuration ( that are fueled by Willpower and does not require Vitae ), kidnapping a lowlife without troubles would be a kid's play. Even better, he could buy illegal immigrants from a human trader, or simply trick or kidnap them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A ghoul who hunts vampires for vitae is not necessarily a bad idea </div> </div> </div>It already exist in the core rulebook, it's called &quot;fugitive ghoul&quot;. My idea was a ghoul that safely farms vampire and Vitae from kidnapped humans ( way more easier than hunting vampires ).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> @ Nofather: The idea was &quot;something that everyone could potentially do&quot;. Knowing that vampire can sire other vampire is... well, &quot;basic&quot;, knowledge. Controlling a young, comparatively weak vampire with steel bounds and obstructions for sight, speak, claws and fangs is something that a Jigsaw-minded character with a basament, a little resources and a lot of time is reasonably able to do. Kidnapping hookers, homeless and illegal foreigners from a large area is not a big problem for a mundane serial killer and a joke for a Ghoul. Also, staying far away from large cities would be quite good for avoiding attention from vampire society ( and ONLY a ghoul could do that ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-17-2015, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T15:20:24-07:00","id":705771,"title":"","content":"From the number of measures you're describing it doesn't come across as &quot;way easier than hunting vampires.&quot; It comes across as needlessly opaque and likely to explode in your ghoul's face.<br /> <br /> Also, I know about the fugitive ghoul. Ghoul hunters go all the way back to the first edition Masquerade supplement Hunter's Hunted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T15:26:00-07:00","id":705782,"title":"","content":"@Resplendent Fire:<br /> <br /> Think about that: what is more risky?<br /> <br /> Controlling a new-embraced vampire that knows nothing about his powers and is chained and caged in a basement in the midst of the desert ( away from big cities ), a vampire that has 3 dots in Disciplines you already know and can't come up with anything new;<br /> <br /> or hunting new vampires every month, in medium-to-large cities were any kind of trouble can bring police attention on you, with the ever present risk to be ripped to pieces by an Ancilla or even by a Neonate that have a Discipline you never saw before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-17-2015, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T15:28:32-07:00","id":705783,"title":"","content":"Also, I really recommend reading the &quot;Integrity&quot; bit in the God-Machine Chronicle sourcebook... I suspect few humans would have a morality wherein it's perfectly okay to abduct people and turn them into vampires for one's own personal gain. If the embrace is an automatic humanity <i>loss, </i>not even a breaking point, then it's probably going to have a pretty corrosive effect on your notional ghoul's integrity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T15:32:50-07:00","id":705787,"title":"","content":"I use the first edition Morality rules. Kidnapping humans in order to turn them undead, enslave, torture and kill them would be...<br /> well, I guess that would be a Morality 0 character, like a Slasher.<br /> <br /> Using Hunter / Slasher alternative morality, mabye a Morality 1-3 character with a Code.<br /> <br /> <br /> But, really, I'm searching for flaws in the plan. If there are weak points I wish to know them.<br /> In your opinion, a human turned into vampire, without proper training, could be still able to manage an escape from a well-designed prison?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T15:41:19-07:00","id":705790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=705782#post705782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Resplendent Fire:<br /> <br /> Think about that: what is more risky?<br /> <br /> Controlling a new-embraced vampire that knows nothing about his powers and is chained and caged in a basement in the midst of the desert ( away from big cities ), a vampire that has 3 dots in Disciplines you already know and can't come up with anything new;<br /> <br /> or hunting new vampires every month, in medium-to-large cities were any kind of trouble can bring police attention on you, with the ever present risk to be ripped to pieces by an Ancilla or even by a Neonate that have a Discipline you never saw before?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, you're talking about this ghoul running a human trafficking operation in order to feed that ghoul's desire for immortality. This is aside from the torture and and premeditated murder that you're committing.<br /> <br /> So at what point does kidnapping <i>not</i> attract attention? Even if you're abducting people who you think are less likely to be missed, this doesn't mean they won't be missed, or that you won't be impinging on a Kindred's feeding ground, or that kidnapping is going to go smoothly just because you want it to.<br /> <br /> Then you get to the torture. You're torturing a vampire into embracing a human. So, that's a) torture, and b) you're torturing this guy so he'll kill someone for you. Your vaunted jaw lock thingy <i>has</i> to come off if you want the embrace to happen at all, and you're going to have a pissed off Kindred with a virtually full blood pool after he drains the human you've given him. How are you going to get the lock back on exactly, without being bitten or outright attacked? Heck - how are you getting it off without getting near the vampire unless you make some kind of Rube Goldberg monstrosity that's as likely to break as work?<br /> <br /> And then there's dealing with the &quot;used&quot; vampires, setting them aside staked or outright killing them, neither of which is a particularly morally neutral act - especially when you are causing harm to someone you have a first stage blood bond to (Integrity -2 breaking point).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T15:50:37-07:00","id":705811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So at what point does kidnapping <i>not</i> attract attention? Even if you're abducting people who you think are less likely to be missed, this doesn't mean they won't be missed, or that you won't be impinging on a Kindred's feeding ground, or that kidnapping is going to go smoothly just because you want it to. </div> </div> </div>Actually, even if an illegal immigrant is missed, his disappearance isn't &quot;unlikely&quot; to be reported: It simply cannot be reported to the police, because those who reports it would be arrested.<br /> <br /> About impinging a Kindred's feeding ground, this is impossible because Kindreds (un)live in medium-to-large cities. People from streets, service stations and isolated locations ( like in the supplement Midnight Roads ) can't imping a Kindred domain simply because there are no Kindreds outside cities ( at least, that I read from Vampire The Requiem corebook ).<br /> <br /> About the kidnapping going smoothly, yes, there is a measure of risk...<br /> <br /> but, honestly, what is more risky: hunting a vampire in a city ( where if you make too much noise you draw attention from police, and you can pick a too strong vampire, and provoke the revenge of other vampires ), or kidnapping a lonely human hitchicker on a secondary street 100 miles away from the nearest city?<br /> Also, so far from a city, it's virtually impossible to mistakenly try kidnap a vampire or a ghoul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then you get to the torture. You're torturing a vampire into embracing a human. So, that's a) torture, and b) you're torturing this guy so he'll kill someone for you. Your vaunted jaw lock thingy <i>has</i> to come off if you want the embrace to happen at all, and you're going to have a pissed off Kindred with a virtually full blood pool after he drains the human you've given him. How are you going to get the lock back on exactly, without being bitten or outright attacked? Heck - how are you getting it off without getting near the vampire unless you make some kind of Rube Goldberg monstrosity that's as likely to break as work? </div> </div> </div>Mabye the fact that I think about first edition and you about second created some misunderstanding. In first edition, a Strenght 5, Vigor 1 vampire can't bend a steel bar. He can break bone, crash a solid wooden door, but bending steel is the kind of thing an elder ( or a war-form Werewolf ) does, and with effort.<br /> <br /> About the jaw locker, what's the problem? Stick in the heart from safe distance ( crossbow or ten-feet wooden pole ), put on the jaw locker, remove the stick, revive the vampire with some pig blood poured in the throat with a syringe ( tracheostomy; no need to remove the jaw locker to feed him )<br /> <br /> All the Ghoul has to do is to chain the vampire's neck to a steel lever that bends only foward and not aside. The vampire would be able to bend slightly the head to bite but he would not be able to turn the neck without breaking steel chains. Then, there is no need to free him when it's time to give the blood to the agonizing human: you just slit his wrist leaving him chained and let the Vitae pour.<br /> The vampire would not be able in any moment to bite, simply because he can't move the neck. Much less to attack ( arms and body chained ).<br /> <br /> Now, mabye a robust vampire ( strenght 4 ) with 3 dots of Vigor that uses all his blood pool to pump his Strenght to 6 and then ( with Vigor ) to 9 COULD be able to bend several thick steel chains at once... but it will takes it several rounds. The Ghoul has all the time to put a stick in his heart, chain him better, revive him with some blood, then torture him in horrible ways to make him reconsider his behiavour, then try again.<br /> <br /> Or, when he notice the vampire is struggling with the chains he takes a step backward, turn up the electricity and roast him a bit.<br /> <br /> But, since vampires still feel fear and pain, I think few would risk doing this kind of attempts while chained, fully knowing that the Ghoul could cut, burn and elletrocute them at will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-17-2015, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T16:10:41-07:00","id":705832,"title":"","content":"Since you're using first edition rules, your serial killer will be dripping with derangements (which is a terrible rule and one of the best things 2e does is eliminate that) from all the premeditated murder and torture.<br /> <br /> You're right, if you have a perfect knowledge of where kindred are you can find the places they aren't and abduct from there. You can even make a reasonable guess, so you're much more likely to attract human authorities.<br /> <br /> And yes, it is possible to report crimes committed against undocumented immigrants. It's not legal to do whatever you want to them and it is not illegal to report crimes <i>against</i> them. And participating in human trafficking could get you into an unreasonable amount of trouble.<br /> <br /> Your plan <i>might</i> work if your serial killer ghoul can read the rulebook, which is how you're determining what to do. There probably isn't a human in the world of darkness who has the kind of information on kindred that one might get by reading the rulebook.<br /> <br /> Like your character isn't going to have an encyclopedic knowledge of how Majesty, Dominate, Nightmare, Obfuscate, etc. work, let alone able to pick out which kindred are likely to have those disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T16:34:29-07:00","id":705849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're right, if you have a perfect knowledge of where kindred are you can find the places they aren't and abduct from there. You can even make a reasonable guess, so you're much more likely to attract human authorities </div> </div> </div>May I make an objection?<br /> If I had to take a guess on how a vampire would hide, I would say &quot;large cities&quot; simply because vampire bites, disappearances and strange behiavour would be noticed everywere else.<br /> <br /> But <i>even with no idea of that</i>, don't you agree that if you have to kidnap someone and you can travel, it's 100 times safer to pick up an hooker or kidnap an hitchicker far from the city than trying to do that inside a city? Cities have cameras everywere, thousand of potential witness at every corner, police patrol that may arrive in minutes, and if you live there you are likely to be recognized someway. Also, after the second or third disappearance in the same area, suspect start rising. And how about the disposal of the body? Even if you hide it in a sewer or throw it in the ocean there are chances it will pop up first or later.<br /> <br /> In open areas, like desert or plains? You just have to dig and forget it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your plan <i>might</i> work if your serial killer ghoul can read the rulebook, which is how you're determining what to do. There probably isn't a human in the world of darkness who has the kind of information on kindred that one might get by reading the rulebook. </div> </div> </div>Well...<br /> since a human get the basic information that vampires exist, what are the more common powers attributed to them?<br /> Superstrenght, superspeed, supertoughness, hypnosis, transformation. If, without further informations, I had to deal with a similar monster ( aside from killing him from 2 km with an elephant riftle ) , I guess I would cover it with chains and block his sight and speaking with something like an helmet. Then , If I had to ask him something, I would push ( with a wooden pole ) a pencil and some paper near his chained hand and tell him to write. That are the basics.<br /> There is no need to know in detail about the disciplines to understand that a monster with hypnotic power and supervillainous strenght has to be locked in steel and prevented to see and speak.<br /> <br /> The more specific informations ( about vinculum, enthrallment and embrace ) would require to have been a ghoul.<br /> That, or months of careful experiments and interrogation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-17-2015, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T16:43:19-07:00","id":705856,"title":"","content":"I think the serial abduction is the weakest link. Really, if the Ghoul has someone they can trust, I'd just place them in charge of keeping the Vampire farm in operation (in an undisclosed-to-the-ghoul location) and send out the blood. Vinculum is little use when the subject doesn't really know where/who their Regnant <i>is</i>. Then you just need to stock the animal blood, and only cycle through a new Vampire every 100 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T16:58:08-07:00","id":705881,"title":"","content":"Thanks Vent0. ^^<br /> I thought about that option, but it would mean to put his life on another's person hands, and a serial killer ghoul likely is a bit too much paranoid for trusting someone else.<br /> <br /> Although the Vinculum fades off after 25 years, so, if he gets to know that, he would need only (25 years to fade x 4 yearly Vitae ) about 100 vampires on sticks to get a steady, permanent and safe Vitae supply. He could even let them sticked forever ( in the corebook I read they can be feed, and dried, even while on torpor ).<br /> <br /> 100 abductions are quite a lot of work, but some serial killers managed to do even better before getting caught. I guess the feat would be possible for a Ghoul that delays it over a long time ( 100- 200 years ) and care to take victims from very distant locations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since you're using first edition rules, your serial killer will be dripping with derangements (which is a terrible rule and one of the best things 2e does is eliminate that) from all the premeditated murder and torture. </div> </div> </div>I always liked alienation sistem ^^<br /> Well, let's think about that.<br /> <br /> For an heinous crime, the derangement throw is 2 dices. It makes roughly a 50% chance of developing a derangement. If the Ghoul is a meticoulous, controlled person, he will take time to use Meditation to prepare himself and rationalize his actions ( following the rules, that is a + 1 bonus on the derangement throw ). That turns the 50% probability into a 34 %. It means more or less one alienation every 3 points of Morality loss.<br /> <br /> He would probably be a Morality 5 character due other, lesser crimes before he starts the project ( due stalking, premeditating, creating an illegal basement / torture room ). Lesser crimes grant more dices, so it's statistically unlikely he'll get derangements before falling to Morality 4 or less.<br /> <br /> In the end, at Morality zero, he would likely have 1 to 3 alienations.<br /> <br /> Narcissism, Suspicion, mabye Blood Fascination. It would be a self centered, unhempatetic egotist that relies only on himself and enjoys really much the sight of both vampiric and normal blood. Nothing that makes him less functional or efficent. Kinda cool in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-17-2015, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T17:32:15-07:00","id":705920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=705745#post705745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> and so on. Coercing with fire and starvation a neonate that knows nothing about vampirism should be quite easy.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Uhhh, provoking a brand new vampire who doesn't understand the Beast is <b>not</b> in a ghoul's best interest. Come to think of it, what ensures the new vampire even knows how to sire anybody?<br /> <br /> As for the blood bond, apparently it wears off after a year, right? And Ghouls only need to drink vitae once a month. So if you keep six vampires around, you can rotate them every 2 months and stave off the blood bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T17:42:48-07:00","id":705932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=705920#post705920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Uhhh, provoking a brand new vampire who doesn't understand the Beast is <b>not</b> in a ghoul's best interest. Come to think of it, what ensures the new vampire even knows how to sire anybody?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume it's an intuitive thing, something you can kinda sorta grasp without teaching, even if you fumble it a little bit and end up making an awkward mess. Like with sex. Or murder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T17:43:52-07:00","id":705933,"title":"","content":"That neonate would be chained and quite helpless, Nyrufa.<br /> The new vampire would not know the procedure, but the Ghould would know and teach it to him ( &quot;drain him, let your blood pour, then focus your will like you're shredding your soul in him&quot; ).<br /> <br /> The blood bond requires a blood potency decay ( 25 years ), it takes more than 6 vampires. One hundred at least, following my calculations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T17:55:04-07:00","id":705946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=705745#post705745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ Nofather: The idea was &quot;something that everyone could potentially do&quot;. Knowing that vampire can sire other vampire is... well, &quot;basic&quot;, knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the problem. Not all vampires sire other vampires in a similar method. If you catch a Jiangshi, you will need an operating table and a good person. If you capture a Qedesha, any man they try to Embrace will die. And from there, how would 'everyone' be able to tell whether the vampire is faking it or not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Controlling a young, comparatively weak vampire with steel bounds and obstructions for sight, speak, claws and fangs is something that a Jigsaw-minded character with a basament, a little resources and a lot of time is reasonably able to do. </div> </div> </div>Vampires do not wear palm flowers that announce their age to people. And vampires don't have to be old to master obscure and powerful disciplines that could, for example, allow them to escape steel bounds and obstructions. Unless you have their character sheet, you will not know what they are capable of. Even spying on them would only show you what they did within the time you spied upon them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kidnapping hookers, homeless and illegal foreigners from a large area is not a big problem for a mundane serial killer and a joke for a Ghoul. Also, staying far away from large cities would be quite good for avoiding attention from vampire society ( and ONLY a ghoul could do that ). </div> </div> </div>Since you don't have the Invictus backing you up, it can be a pretty big deal for a mundane serial killer or ghoul. If you stay away from large cities you aren't as likely to come across hookers and homeless to kidnap, not to mention the fact that vampires are not bound to large cities and there are plenty that avoid them entirely, even bloodlines based on the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T18:27:54-07:00","id":705994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=705881#post705881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Vent0. ^^<br /> I thought about that option, but it would mean to put his life on another's person hands, and a serial killer ghoul likely is a bit too much paranoid for trusting someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the Ghoul <i>already</i> a serial killer? Because using the proxy method, they don't <i>have </i>to be. They only need to abduct/Embrace once every 100 year per vampire, which keeps the numbers rather low. Heck, they would be less of an invasive impact than the Kindred themselves.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T18:44:54-07:00","id":706019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is the problem. Not all vampires sire other vampires in a similar method. If you catch a Jiangshi, you will need an operating table and a good person. If you capture a Qedesha, any man they try to Embrace will die. And from there, how would 'everyone' be able to tell whether the vampire is faking it or not? </div> </div> </div>I don't know these bloodlines, but in most game... first edition games, at least... bloodlines are a tiny minority. Even &quot;major&quot; bloodlines ( Brujah, Toreador, Malkavian ) are a minority, and since entering a bloodline requires a Blood Potency of at least 2, many vampires do not even qualify. Yes, theorically speaking one could randomly meet a unique bloodline vampire, but - at least in the game I used to play - 90% of vampires are standard Ventrue, Daeva, Nosferatu, Gangrel and Meketh, around 9% Brujah, Toreador and Malkavian, and less than 1% stranger things.<br /> <br /> How tell if he's faking?<br /> <br /> &quot; Listen well, bloodsucker. Now you sire that dude. If he don't rise up after you have done with him, I'll burn your left hand fingers one at time. &quot; And, just to be sure he understand, you burn him a bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since you don't have the Invictus backing you up, it can be a pretty big deal for a mundane serial killer or ghoul. If you stay away from large cities you aren't as likely to come across hookers and homeless to kidnap, not to mention the fact that vampires are not bound to large cities and there are plenty that avoid them entirely, even bloodlines based on the concept. </div> </div> </div>Real life serial killer that were lucid enough to travel between crimes usually were caught only after scoring dozen of victims.<br /> A Ghoul have several heavy advantages over a mundane serial killer: if he get hurts, even badly, he can heal himself without ospitalization; if he needs to do, he can muster unhuman strenght and agility; he doesn't age, so he had not to worry with loss of lucidity and health over the decades. And if he have even a single dot of Majesty or Domination from his sire, he can effortlessly persuade an hooker or hitchiker to come in his van and take a ( chloroformed ) beer without any struggle. If he have a single dot of Obscuration he's virtually undetectable ( for a single victim ). One dot of Animalism and he can use wild birds to detect an potential witness or danger.<br /> <br /> About preys, gas stations and road motel are usually visited by hookers, tourists and travellers. Sure, a tourist will probably have a family, but it's extremely hard for police to understand when and where exactly an highway traveller disappeared because a few hours may mean hundreds of miles of difference. That's the reason most people that disappear during long travels are never found.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires do not wear palm flowers that announce their age to people. And vampires don't have to be old to master obscure and powerful disciplines that could, for example, allow them to escape steel bounds and obstructions. Unless you have their character sheet, you will not know what they are capable of. Even spying on them would only show you what they did within the time you spied upon them.\u200b </div> </div> </div>I don't know what to say. When I played as a vampire, it happened to me to be kidnapped by a gang of thugs, and I had to be rescued by my cotheire despite being a mid-low level character ( several sessions, around 20-22 xp, plus 10 for lowering to 5 my starting humanity ). Mabye the first edition is a lower-power gamestyle.<br /> <br /> Anyway, YES, the first step, capturing the first vampire, is definetly the most dangerous. The Ghoul would need to apply Hunter-like tactiques to get his first pray.<br /> <br /> The best solution that comes in my mind is to arrange a trap and have the vampire locked somewhere, like an abandoned building with thick walls and locked, reinforced doors, then spy him with binoculars. Even better, with a little cam hidden inside the building. If he manage to tear down walls and reinforced doors, or he transform himself into gas and fly away, or do anything else spectacular, he's too strong. If he's locked in and unable to escape, after a couple of days the Ghoul can shoot him into torpor using a riftled with noise suppressor ( from a sniper-hole ). Or wait he's in an hunger frenzy and throw in a drugged bag of blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> not to mention the fact that vampires are not bound to large cities and there are plenty that avoid them entirely, even bloodlines based on the concept.\u200b </div> </div> </div>I don't know. In the first edition Vampire The Requiem core rulebook it's written in an extremely clear way that the overwhelming majority of vampires fear travelling outside due werewolf threat, scarcity of blood and logistic problems. The only exception in the core book is the clan Brujah, that is a small and relatively young bloodline. In a standard, first edition game the travelling vampire is the exception, and a rare one.<br /> <br /> But, anyway, as a rule of prudence, Ghouls should move in the day hours when they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-17-2015, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T19:11:48-07:00","id":706056,"title":"","content":"Does this thought experiment serve a purpose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T19:15:09-07:00","id":706061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=706019#post706019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Real life serial killer that were lucid enough to travel between crimes usually were caught only after scoring dozen of victims.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't living for centuries without aging part of the point of being an independent ghoul like this? This doesn't sound like a short-term plan, and an abnormal disappearance rate is going to build up over time. That's why I gauged the annual rate: because this plan kind of doesn't sound worth it unless it sustains you for a <i>long</i> time. If &quot;a dozen victims&quot; is a mark of high success and you're kidnapping a bare minimum of two people every year, you haven't even bought yourself ten years of immortality before you're pushing it. Double your high water mark for the advantages of being a ghoul and you stall old age by a little over one decade before you start to worry. And that's with estimates working heavily in your favor.<br /> <br /> Like... okay, what are you <i>doing</i> with your ghouldom in the interim between kidnappings and making sure your vampire captives don't escape and seek revenge, that makes it worth the trouble?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T19:19:46-07:00","id":706064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=705651#post705651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know how it works in second edition. In first edition NWod, a Ghoul requires 1 monthly point of Vitae to stay a Ghoul. Assuming he has decent constitution ( 3 ) and drink from every vampire once, he needs to kidnap one human every 3 months. It's way less collateral damage than the average vampire does.<br /> <br /> About the animal blood, it's 60 lts / months. Slaughterhouses routinely throws gallons of blood every months and manage to sell just a small part of it. Also, with a bit of resources, having a few pigs and/or cows and taking small quantities of blood from them would do the job.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Majesty isn't mind control, it can't force a subject to do a blatantly suicidal action ( like unrestrain the vampire ). That would require Domination ( that requires hearing an eye contact ). Also, it's possible to reflexively spend Willpower to resist Majesty and there are heavy bonuses if the vampire is an enemy (+1 ) and if it poses a deadly threat (+2 ). The Ghould could keep a remote control at hand and non-lethally ( but painfully ) elettrocute the vampire at the first hint he's using tricks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To reach an arm you would need to move more-or-less the jaws. With a jaw locker and head bound by chains there's literally no way to do that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Claw through steel? To do that, even moving freely, I would require at least Strenght 7-8 or several dots in Vigor. But a vampire with vrists and arms bound by steel chains can't move his claws enough to reach the chains and cut them. He would have to break the chains with brute force, that would be possible for an elder, mabye.<br /> <br /> Other options ( protean powers ) would seriously put in danger the warden, but they're advanced powers. I was thinking about abducting a young, relatively powerless vampire.<br /> Clearly, anything stronger than a Neonate would be able to escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the def of those manacles? Ancient nosferatu trick could get thru them.<br /> BTW while you are torturing your victim you are putting him/her in an emotionally stressfull situation. As a an ST I would give his sire, Grandsire, childe, and grandchilde a blood ties check everytime you hit the victim with a hot poker. If it was second hell half the clan would know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T19:32:18-07:00","id":706093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does this thought experiment serve a purpose? </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about a fanfiction.<br /> <br /> @Stupid Loserman<br /> <br /> I've said dozens, not &quot;a dozen&quot;. Take a look.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_serial_killers_by_number_of_victims#Serial_killers_with_the_highest_known_victim_count\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_o...n_victim_count</a><br /> <br /> All done by normal, mundane men. Most of them committed their crimes in a short time-span, much shorter that 10 years.<br /> <br /> Also, I doubt that 10, or even 100 disappearances from different locations would raise heat, if no bodies are ever found. It has been extimated that something around a million people disappear in US every year. Obviously, most of them aren't death: the majority are runaway that, for a reason or another, lose or deliberately interrupt contacts with relatives and acuaintances. 100 people disappearing in a single city would spread panic; but if they disappear in different cities or highways, they would be less than 1/ 1000 of the total disappearances of a single state. Spread around 5 or 10 states, it would be a leaf in a forest.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like... okay, what are you <i>doing</i> with your ghouldom in the interim between kidnappings and making sure your vampire captives don't escape and seek revenge, that makes it worth the trouble? </div> </div> </div><br /> Captives escaping and seeking revenge? No way. When you have the information you need and they have done the Embracing thing, stick on the heart and they sleep in torpor. Pig blood can be syringed in their throat and Vitae out of their bodies without pulling out the stick. <br /> <br /> About what doing in the spare time...<br /> <br /> Well, that is a matter of personal tastes. Everyone has their own hobbies. ^^<br /> Seriously, that ghould would have plenty of time and freedom to exercise his disciplines, expecially those which does not require Vitae expenditure. Or do mundane training and study, becoming more and more powerful and knowledgeable. When he collected around 100 kidnappings, after 25 years, he can even stop hunting and simply enjoy eternal life. Or &quot;farm&quot; some other vampires to have an extra supply he can use to pratice Vigor, Celerity and Resilience, and bring them to 5 dots since he doesn't require a teacher for them.<br /> <br /> Supernatural powers, eternal youth, no masters and the thrill of the hunt... it sounds quite appealing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-17-2015, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T19:55:20-07:00","id":706132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=705745#post705745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> @ Nofather: The idea was &quot;something that everyone could potentially do&quot;. Knowing that vampire can sire other vampire is... well, &quot;basic&quot;, knowledge. Controlling a young, comparatively weak vampire with steel bounds and obstructions for sight, speak, claws and fangs is something that a Jigsaw-minded character with a basament, a little resources and a lot of time is reasonably able to do. Kidnapping hookers, homeless and illegal foreigners from a large area is not a big problem for a mundane serial killer and a joke for a Ghoul. Also, staying far away from large cities would be quite good for avoiding attention from vampire society ( and ONLY a ghoul could do that ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? How does your ghoul know how vamps make other vamps? Even Horror literature is all over the map.<br /> <br /> Again even a neonate Nos with the right devotion will get out of those restraints in time. They have one that lets them ignore the up to their BP in defense of an object when using vigor.<br /> Also don't overlook Bloodties though in First edition there is a range limit without certain circle ritual.<br /> Actually you would do better under second edition collecting revenants with an easier blood use rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T19:57:49-07:00","id":706136,"title":"","content":"Mh...<br /> I just remembered a thing I read in the Ghoul supplement for The Requiem. Ghouls are still subject to diseases. Although it should not be a big problem, the Ghoul should simply buy medical equipement, get a couple dots in Medicine and do some blood exams to his victims before allowing the vampires to turn them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Off topic question: what is the average survival of independent ghouls? I guess a year or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-17-2015, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T19:58:54-07:00","id":706137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=706019#post706019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know these bloodlines, but in most game... first edition games, at least... bloodlines are a tiny minority. Even &quot;major&quot; bloodlines ( Brujah, Toreador, Malkavian ) are a minority, and since entering a bloodline requires a Blood Potency of at least 2, many vampires do not even qualify. Yes, theorically speaking one could randomly meet a unique bloodline vampire, but - at least in the game I used to play - 90% of vampires are standard Ventrue, Daeva, Nosferatu, Gangrel and Meketh, around 9% Brujah, Toreador and Malkavian, and less than 1% stranger things.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's your setting that's your setting, but even there rogue ghouls are even less common and if you're talking about someone with the infrastructure to take masses of people from one place to another where they're kept captive you're talking about a lot of travel through the territories of other vampires. Simple fact is the Embrace isn't always as easy as biting someone to death, and a ghoul wouldn't have the experience to know this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Real life serial killer that were lucid enough to travel between crimes usually were caught only after scoring dozen of victims.<br /> A Ghoul have several heavy advantages over a mundane serial killer: if he get hurts, even badly, he can heal himself without ospitalization; if he needs to do, he can muster unhuman strenght and agility; he doesn't age, so he had not to worry with loss of lucidity and health over the decades. And if he have even a single dot of Majesty or Domination from his sire, he can effortlessly persuade an hooker or hitchiker to come in his van and take a ( chloroformed ) beer without any struggle. If he have a single dot of Obscuration he's virtually undetectable ( for a single victim ). One dot of Animalism and he can use wild birds to detect an potential witness or danger.<br /> <br /> About preys, gas stations and road motel are usually visited by hookers, tourists and travellers. Sure, a tourist will probably have a family, but it's extremely hard for police to understand when and where exactly an highway traveller disappeared because a few hours may mean hundreds of miles of difference. That's the reason most people that disappear during long travels are never found. </div> </div> </div>I see you found the wiki page, did you notice how few of the serial killers with dozens of victims managed to make it into the 21st century in the United States? And that'd discounting an entire subsociety of undead magic people who leap to attention when a body is found drained of blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know. In the first edition Vampire The Requiem core rulebook it's written in an extremely clear way that the overwhelming majority of vampires fear travelling outside due werewolf threat, scarcity of blood and logistic problems. The only exception in the core book is the clan Brujah, that is a small and relatively young bloodline. In a standard, first edition game the travelling vampire is the exception, and a rare one. </div> </div> </div>There's <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1590/Nomads\" target=\"_blank\">an entire book</a> devoted to it, one of the better supplements. The 'fear of werewolves' thing is an artifact of Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fanfiction. </div> </div> </div>Well in that case, 'How would a ghoul coerce a vampire to embrace someone' may have been a better way to word it, since in your story its possibility or impossibility is already decided. I want to point out I'm not saying, 'No.' I think I made it clear in my other post that yes, it can happen, and probably does happen I'm just pointing out obstacles someone who did this would run into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T20:07:07-07:00","id":706140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm just pointing out obstacles someone who did this would run into. </div> </div> </div>It's exactly what I needed and I'm grateful to you and the other users that helped my in that brainstorming since now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Although honestly I had not already decided if the possibility was real or not when I started the topic because I had doubt about the possibility to coerce the Embrace, not the logistical possibility of it. I suspected it's such a ... &quot;personal&quot; act that mabye it could not be done if the vampire don't honestly want it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I found a lot of inspiration in that conversation. I like problem-solving.<br /> <br /> Ah, thanks about the Nomad supplement, I'll try to download it if I can find it freeware. I used mainly Midnight Roads for that thought exercise.<br /> <br /> @Chattnos:<br /> <br /> Definetly YES , it would be risky and full of uncertainity, the first time. A clever Ghoul should test the vampire by luring him into a simple trap ( abandoned building with thick walls and metal doors ), and try to capture him only if he's clearly a weakling that is unable to escape from a locked building.<br /> Then, when he manage to capture a weakling, he would have to scare him enough to make him Embrance a kidnapped victim, so the Ghoul can learn the procedure.<br /> <br /> It's difficult and complicated. But, at least in my opinion, way safer than hunt every time a new vampire. Basically, after the first time, it's done. The successive vampire would be even weaker and all of the same lineage, that means no unespected powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-17-2015, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T22:16:31-07:00","id":706344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=705933#post705933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That neonate would be chained and quite helpless, Nyrufa.<br /> The new vampire would not know the procedure, but the Ghould would know and teach it to him ( &quot;drain him, let your blood pour, then focus your will like you're shredding your soul in him&quot; ).<br /> <br /> The blood bond requires a blood potency decay ( 25 years ), it takes more than 6 vampires. One hundred at least, following my calculations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wait, is that a second or first gen rule? I could have sworn I read that 1 year without drinking your master's blood severs the bond. That or slaying them.<br /> <br /> <br /> If it's as you say, then yes. It would be a hell of a lot easier to just get yourself turned and have your own, renewable vitae supply than to kill a hundred people just to live another year.<br /> <br /> And when I mentioned the vampire severing its appendages to break free, keep in mind that even novice vampires can often muster the strength to rip a human to shreds. Is it so impossible then they could rip themselves out of their bindings such as dislocating their joints or just fly into a Frenzy and snap it off at the bone?<br /> <br /> Assuming a human has a strength level of 1 (40 lbs), the first level of Vigor is still going to give you the strength to lift 100 lbs. A second point in vigor raises it to 250, the third point to 400, the fourth point to 650 and at mastery you can lift 800 lbs. That's just with a basic, Strength 1 human, now imagine that with somebody who frequently works out and is in healthy condition. Also keep in mind that upon becoming a vampire, the character automatically gets an increase to a clan favored attribute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-18-2015, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T22:27:04-07:00","id":706346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it's as you say, then yes. It would be a hell of a lot easier to just get yourself turned and have your own, renewable vitae supply than to kill a hundred people just to live another year. </div> </div> </div>No, no. I explained myself unclearly.<br /> Four people would be needed to live one year.<br /> <br /> One hundred people turned into vampires and cicled would provide Vitae for live forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T22:55:58-07:00","id":706377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=706346#post706346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, no. I explained myself unclearly.<br /> Four people would be needed to live one year.<br /> <br /> One hundred people turned into vampires and cicled would provide Vitae for live forever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think by that point, one of several things can happen<br /> <br /> <br /> 1 - You're whoring the vamps out to the renegade Ghoul population.<br /> <br /> 2 - The Sheriff kicks down your door and goes postal on your operations.<br /> <br /> 3 - Hunters come looking for you, probably not in the hopes of recruiting.<br /> <br /> 4 - The vampires subject you to the embrace, lock you in a coffin and weld the locks shut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T09:07:41-07:00","id":706980,"title":"","content":"Way i see it, the greatest complication with maitaining such an operation would be:<br /> <br /> 1) Correctly gauging a vampire's individual power level is not always simple even for kindred, that have something of a sensitivity to it, much more so for a ghoul or mortal, not to mention one might get unlucky and come across a paranoid and inhumanly observant one (Mekhets being particularly prone to this combo, in fact) that may catch on to someone stalking them (and prepare itself accordingly) <b>before</b> one is even sure of wanting to taking them down, what can complicate somewhat things.<br /> <br /> 2) Blood Sympathy connects a vampire to their &quot;blood relations&quot;, read, their sires, grandsires, childer and grandchilder, all of whom have a chance of catching glimpses of any emotionally-charged situations a kindred goes through - like being attacked, staked and tortured into compulsory embrace and becoming someone's vitae factory. It ain't anywhere close to reliable, but the longer one messes with a captured vampire, the greater are chances of some &quot;relative&quot; trying to track them down, or getting help of those with an interest in that kind of disturbance, like hounds and sheriffs.<br /> <br /> And for the sake of reference, it doesn't take an ancilla or elder to have grandchilder: neonate A embraces neonate B because it was feeling really miserable and needed the company of a friend/lover. A few years, months, damn, even as little as a few weeks later, neonate B goes on and embraces neonate C, one's best bud since forever who was about to have a miserable, painful end due to a drive-by, car accident or disease on terminal stage and B decided to give fate the finger. So, depending on circunstances, there could be between 0-4+ kindred of the same city who occasionally get glimpses of weird crap going on and might be looking for them, per kindred one captured straight from the streets.<br /> <br /> Damn, the ghoul's system you have given so far sort of digs itself an even bigger hole in a way, as every hobo/hooker/drifter/illegal immigrant/etc embraced is one more undead prisioner under regular imprisonment and torture with a blood tie to another undead prisioner. What means your prisioners will be at least aware of each other's existence and might try to find ways to help each other or complicate their wardens lives, not to mention the whole emotional hoopla involved in their whole situation might lead them in who knows what weird mental paths and things blowing up into crap like the Barjot's or even worse, Melissidae's brand of hive mind would not be out of the realm of possibility. One could end up with some sort of weird brand new bloodline being born or even worse surprises into one's hands without wanting to.<br /> <br /> 3) Zoo maintenance - simply put, serial killers usually have being killers in their favor - they kill people, throw the corpse somewhere to rot and move on, rinse and repeat. Meanwhile the ghoul <b>can't</b> do the same with the kindred, because it's milking them out of the all too important vitae they produce. So, not only does one never rid oneself of one's corpses (because they are one's cash cow so to speak), but one needs a whole operation to keep them imprisoned and reliably producing vitae and will look for every chance of escape they can.<br /> <br /> And because one needs a variety of vitae sources to try to forestall any vinculum formation, obtaining ever more animate corpses - through straight capture or coerced embrace of random people - becomes a necessity and the more kindred you have, the greater becomes one's requirements for space arrangements to keep them caged (not to mention the cells, restraints &amp; etc), access &amp; expenditures into sources of animal blood, boxes or cellars for torpid ones, &quot;jailors&quot; that must be paid of for their service, in vitae possibly (as i have difficulty of thinking of much beside potential immortality that would be worth such an utterly atrocious job), driving upkeep costs even higher and so on, ever harder to hide effectively as one goes...serious snowball effect there.<br /> <br /> I can see one possible workaround on the last problem, that would be for one to keep one, at most two vampires imprisoned and deal with the &quot;vinculum avoidance&quot; issue by <b>regular trade </b>with other ghouls who are similarly taking care of only one or two young kindred. That way one only needs to dedicate the time and resources for one or two prisioners - much more manageable, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fritzl_case\" target=\"_blank\">as real life</a> shows us <a href=\"http://www.theguardian.com/world/2011/aug/25/austrian-father-accused-imprisoning-daughters\" target=\"_blank\">all too awfully well </a>- and <b>keeping one's contact list safe and up to date</b>. Networking things considerably disperses the management costs of the whole operation and might considerably reduce the need for periodic additional embraces, much diminishing most of the other risks, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-28-2023, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T09:22:22-07:00","id":706990,"title":"","content":"@Baaldam:<br /> <br /> I don't know if that works in second edition, but in first edition you can leave a vampire with a stick in his heart, and he's fully unconscious and totally helpless. Also, a vampire can be feed ( and therefore produce Vitae that may then be harvested with a syringe ) without even removing the stick. The only moment a vampire would be conscious would be to Embrace a new one, or to be interrogated / tortured, and only one vampire at time. In every other moment they would all be sticked and in torpor.<br /> <br /> These vampire would be both chained and in torpor with a stick in the heart. I don't see many escaping opportunities. Also, they would not requires cells and spaces, nor jailers or guards; just a battery chicken structure.<br /> <br /> I also guess that keeping all them less one in torpor would solve Blood Simpathy problem ( I don't think that torpor nightmares spread to awake vampires; if that would the case, all vampires in the world would go mad in short time ).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1) Making sure of a vampire's individual power level is not always simple, not to mention one might get unlucky and come across a paranoid and inhumanly observant one (Mekhets being particularly prone to this combo, in fact) that may catch on to someone stalking them (and prepare itself accordingly) <b>before</b> one is even sure of wanting to taking them down, what can<br /> complicate somewhat things </div> </div> </div>This is, definetly, the most riskful part of the plan, I agree.<br /> But, one observation: Hunters and fugitive Ghouls take that risk every single time they hunt. The farming Ghoul would need to take it only one time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can see one possible workaround on the last problem, that would be for one to keep one, at most two vampires imprisoned and deal with the &quot;vinculum avoidance&quot; issue by <b>regular trade </b>with other ghouls who are similarly taking care of only one or two young kindred. </div> </div> </div>Vitae becomes normal blood minutes after being harvested. It can't be traded, at least not by transporting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-18-2015, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T13:23:14-07:00","id":707354,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that a Ghoul really only needs 12 drinks a year. to stay up and running. That is about the only saving grace of this plan. Really what you need is 12+ vampires chained in your basement, staked. Feed them blood through their torpor'd mouth and drain them 1/year.<br /> <br /> That said, draining is the issue. I'm not sure you can take a vamp's blood without fangs unless they give it. Injury doesn't make them blood. If a vamp goes full on 'screw you' they can all clam up without giving you any of their previous blood. That said, I think draining should be possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T14:21:51-07:00","id":707384,"title":"","content":"Just for the sake of the rogue ghoul plotlines I'd say that a ghoul has enough vamp in them that if they manage to cut a vampire and suck on the wound the vitae <i>will</i> come out. <br /> <br /> Also, artificial fangs are probably a thing. Just get some pointy crowns put on your canines by a sufficiently back-alley dentist. Or just file the things into points. The possibilities are endless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T14:28:11-07:00","id":707386,"title":"","content":"A syringe would definetly be more pratical. I remember reading somewhere that most of Vitae is stored in the heart, so I guess that after a bit of pratice, taking it from a vampire in torpor will not be so hard.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T14:35:20-07:00","id":707407,"title":"","content":"Better be quick. From the Blood, p47, 'when Vitae is separated from a vampire\u2019s body, voluntarily or otherwise, after a few moments it reverts back to ordinary blood once again, albeit of an unde\ufb01 ned origin \u2014 human blood, yes, but of no singular type \u2014 and depleted of its original integrity, with a unexplainable breakdown of cells apparent to any skilled observer...'<br /> <br /> And perhaps make sure they're not conscious. P49, 'In fact, Vitae is so obedient that even when a vampire is injured in a fashion that would cause a mortal\u2019s blood to spurt forth, Vitae hesitates, seemingly defying the very laws of physics, unwilling to do anything without a direct order from the vampire to do so. What\u2019s more, for the few moments after Vitae exits a vampire\u2019s body \u2014 prior to reverting back to ordinary blood \u2014 the fluid remains under the authority of the vampire. A severed finger can literally be summoned back to the hand from which it came by the mere will of the injured party.'<br /> <br /> Do you know where you read the thing about it in the heart?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-18-2015, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T15:02:45-07:00","id":707455,"title":"","content":"I remember, it was about a Vicissitude power that make the heart being punctured by the ribcage and explode. I was the Old World of Darkness so forget about it.<br /> <br /> Yep, the idea was taking the blood from an unconscious vampire ( stake in the heart ).<br /> Anyway, in the core rulebook rogue ghouls exist, there is even an example NPC, and in the Ghoul supplement for Requiem it's mentioned that some ghouls kept vampires trapped in concrete and drained them slowly. So, it must be possible to forcibly take the Vitae.<br /> <br /> Mabye it's not even necessary. &quot;Bleed the vitae or I burn you&quot; it's a quite persuasive argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T15:06:32-07:00","id":707480,"title":"","content":"Another thing to note is which kind of vampire will you be hunting for in order to erect the battery farm and how will you deal with the consequences?<br /> <br /> <br /> Gangrel - Their loner mentality would make them a likely subject to go after, but their clan is conditioned to be survivors. As the most savage of the clans, you're going to have a hell of a fight on your hands trying to bring one down.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ventrue - There is always somebody trying to extort or slay a Ventrue, it comes with the burden of leadership. I also would say that the high and mighty Lords would take immediate notice of one of their own suddenly disappearing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mekhet - Good luck finding one to begin with. Even if you do, they're probably already aware of what you're trying to do and have warned the others appropriately.<br /> <br /> <br /> Nosferatu - Again, good luck finding one. If you manage to pull that off, good luck getting out of there with your mind / body intact!<br /> <br /> <br /> Daeva - I'm pretty sure the masters of manipulation would be able to tell if a ghoul was trying to lure them into dropping their guard. A Ghoul who's willing to go Buffolo Bill levels of insanity just to remain immortal probably isn't going to have the willpower necessary to fend off their charms, either.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> As for the vitae stored in the heart, that's not the impression I got. When somebody becomes a vampire, most of their bodily fluids turn into vitae, the exceptions being stuff like saliva or the eye fluids. When they drink blood, it doesn't just go straight to the stomach, it's absorbed throughout the body. You could say the vampire body is 75% blood instead of water now. A starving vampire appears withered and malnourished, while a gluttonous vampire appears bloated and squishy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-18-2015, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T15:25:18-07:00","id":707584,"title":"","content":"A ghoul who did this on awake vampires wouldn't have willpower long. They'd be subject to near constant, free lashing out. If they surrender, the vamp can probably get free (since there is an RP &quot;backing down&quot; required for surrendering).<br /> <br /> Protean is an issue because of the various transformations or just sinking into the floor.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate is an issue because the vamp can just disappear themselves and become unfindable (unless the Ghoul takes that one merit).<br /> <br /> Majesty can manipulate the Ghoul into freeing them.<br /> <br /> Nightmare can intimidate the ghoul into freeing them<br /> <br /> Vigor can just break the chains. So can that one merit to ignore item durability..<br /> <br /> Animalism may get cartoon hijinks going, depending on your setup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T18:08:05-07:00","id":707840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vigor can just break the chains. </div> </div> </div>My Meketh blogger / martial artist, despite having Strenght 3 and a dot of Vigor, had an hard time breaking a solid wooden door. Although I found that quite realistical because in real life, even an olympic champion would simply break his shoulder.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit surprised, when we played as freshly embraced Neonates, we ( players ) felt very vulnerable not only thoward elder vampires ( &quot;helpless&quot; is the better word ) but we were also painfully aware that police enforcements and gangster were deadly dangers too. Sure, we had supernatural power, but only one for every player, and nothing that could save us in every situation. We had to rely on cooperation and preparation in order too survive. So, I grow up with the idea that an unexperienced vampire , although invincible for a single human or ghoul, would fall quite easily against an ambush or a small squad of enemies ( even mortals ).<br /> <br /> When I was captured and I had 4 vitae less, Auspex 3 and Vigor 1 ( teached by my Nosferatu friend ), and those thugs tied me to a chair with thick ropes I thought &quot; Well, WTF I do now?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Probably we played a low-power setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T18:51:13-07:00","id":707930,"title":"","content":"About what I would do to capture a vampire with minimizing risks, assuming I'm an Hunter, a weak Ghoul or simply a mortal character that wants one to study and experiment with...<br /> well, it depends on how much information I got about them.<br /> <br /> To localizate a vampire from a safe distance, I would use an high definition camera and, from an elevate position at the maximum distance ( which is several miles with an electronic camera ) I would record night clubs, discoteques and other noctural recreative places. Every five minutes I would control the recording, searching for people that would appear strangely obfuscate despite the others being recorded clearly. Then I would have to do a drawing of the subject or to memorize his face or anatomy ( that would require some training in visual memory techniques but it's not really hard to do ).<br /> <br /> That would require much time but is a safe method. If I had some more economical resorces, a termic camera ( like those used by zoologists ) would speed up the process a lot allowing me to detect people with unusually low body heat.<br /> <br /> I would try to understand roughly how that vampire moves and if there are others like him which he abitually hang out with, always from a long distance. When I found one that I'm reasonably sure routinely moves alone, I would choose a location that allows me a clear sight, arm myself with an high quality hunting crossbow ( +2 dices for quality equipment ), with a binocular gunsight ( +1 ) and a laser pointer ( +2 ); I would assume diazepam to calm nerves and have a firmer hand ( +2 ); then I would take my time to aim ( +3 ) and to concentrate ( 1 point of Willpower for an extra +3 ), and, finallly, place a wooden quadrell between his shoulders right in his heart from 120 yards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another thing to note is which kind of vampire will you be hunting for in order to erect the battery farm and how will you deal with the consequences? </div> </div> </div>The best way to deal with the consequences of capturing a vampire, if the hunter know nothing about him, would be to immediately left the city, travel a long way and having the alread-prepared prison far from any big ( and even small) tow, in a barren location. Beside Auspex 6+ or strange devotions, I guess it would be impossible to track the kidnapper thousand of miles away, in a bunker lost in the desert.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-18-2015, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T19:29:34-07:00","id":708040,"title":"","content":"Diazepam is not going to make physical actions <i>easier</i>. Have you ever taken it? It's a tranquilizer. It will slow you down and make you sleepy.<br /> <br /> Edit: Dude knows what you want him to know, nvm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-18-2015, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T19:57:52-07:00","id":708071,"title":"","content":"Diazepam is considered doping and banned from olympic skeet competitions because it erases the natural trembling of muscles, allowing a firmirer hand.<br /> <br /> ( also, if I was going to shoot a vampire - even from distance - I think I would need a tranquilizer... )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems like you're having him proceed as if he has perfect knowledge of the Requiem rulebook and that doesn't necessarily follow. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Perfect knowledge&quot; would be knowing in detail every Discipline, Bloodline and Devotion. Knowing about sticks and torpor is &quot;basic knowledge&quot;, the kind of things that I would expect even a ghoul to know after a few years spent serving.<br /> <br /> But if we are are talking about a mortal character, then yes, that would require some researches. A reasonably competent scholar ( Occult 2 and a specialization in vampire mythology ) would be able to know that, at least in some cultures and legends, vampires are paralized and not killed by a wooden object in the hearth. He still would need to perform a direct experiment, anyway; the less risky thing would be to do that from the maximum avaiable distance and from a small van with the engine on and ready to go ( in case the legends are wrong and the guy shrug off the quadrel ).<br /> <br /> <br /> A question, Resplendant Fire. Have you read the supplement Antagonists? I liked it because it showed some characters, monster hunters, that were not like superheroes but more mundane vigilantes. One of them was a girl that lured vampires with sex then fought them using surprise and knives, another one an alcholic crackhead / informatic expert that despite poor health managed to kill several monsters with unpredictable tactics ( like a water pistol ridden with gasoil, or running them down with a modified car ). It was also stated clearly that first or later these hunter would die, when they met a foe that would prove too much for them. <br /> <br /> Yet, they manage to take down some foes so I thought &quot;If that is enough, then with better preparation and better weapons, a relatively safe ambush is possible&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-18-2015, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T20:17:41-07:00","id":708087,"title":"","content":"I removed my bit about you having your guy know everything, but no - stakes and torpor are not basic knowledge <i>unless you're a vampire</i>. Most people in the WoD would know about sunlight because of Hollywood, and that wooden stakes can kill because of Hollywood and the like. They wouldn't know that a stake just paralyzes a vampire nor would they know about ghouls. Admittedly, a renegade ghoul might know these things.<br /> <br /> I think part of the problem I have with your scenario is that it seems like everything just goes perfectly for your dude. There's no real struggle, no real risk for him. He does everything right the first time, has all the information he needs to execute his plan, and has no true chance of failure.<br /> <br /> I haven't read Antagonists, but I have read other stuff. I have no problem with hunters being able to kill vampires. It's <i>dangerous</i> and they could <i>die</i> from a misstep, but they can still win if they pull it off. But what makes it work is the sense that there is risk.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, in first edition The Hunters Hunted for Vampire: The Masquerade, there is a thing about ghouls hunting vampire for blood. Now I don't know if this book is even obtainable at this point, but if you ever get a chance to check it out, it might be of interest.<br /> <br /> Or you could check out the recent The Hunters Hunted II for V20. It probably has some material on the topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-18-2015, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T20:48:50-07:00","id":708118,"title":"","content":"Eh, indeed that story would be a really boring chronicle for most players and is more suited for a novel. The whole idea was about minimizing risks. The point was not to do it right the first time but to never risk diying. The protagonist would probably spend months looking from that termic camera and drawing portraits, before being able to track the routes of one particular abitudinary and lonely vampire, and even then, miss the shot and be forcet to take his van, drive away and start it all again in another city because he could have alerted the local vampire forces ( of whom he knows nothing ).<br /> <br /> The psychology of the character is a bit different from an Hunter. Hunters hate and loath monsters and wants them death, so they take risks in order to take them down. That character wants to live forever and fears death, so he cannot take any risk for his life and have to conceive a plan that, even if fails, don't put him in a position of danger.<br /> <br /> Also, I was thinking what kind of prison would build a reasonably cautious and paranoid character that has to deal with a supernatural monster which could possess powers he doesn't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T20:51:29-07:00","id":708119,"title":"","content":"Well I mean it doesn't sound like an interesting story to read or write, not without complications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T21:16:24-07:00","id":708121,"title":"","content":"Minimizing risk would probably involve submitting to a Regnant and Vinculum and not becoming a mass murderer the likes of which the mortal world has never seen before.<br /> <br /> Just sayin'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T21:51:48-07:00","id":708132,"title":"","content":"Submitting to a Regnant would mean become an expendable pawn to a monster that will almost eventualy go crazier and crazier as he gets older, not to mention the loss of freedom and individuality. Even without knowing that, it would mean put unconditionally your life in the fangs of a literal monster.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T22:40:17-07:00","id":708155,"title":"","content":"Ghouls are not expendable. They require grooming and maintenance and an investment in time and resources. Having a Regnant also provides you with some protection and rights in Vampire society. All in all, it is in every conceivable way safer than everything else proposed in this thread. Independence is a fine goal, but pretending the goal is &quot;minimizing risk&quot; is kind of ludicrous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T22:50:11-07:00","id":708190,"title":"","content":"You are talking about second edition or first edition ghouls?<br /> <br /> Actually, those we met when I was playing were cannon fodder and slaves at best, torture-toys at worst. Beaten, mistreated, randomly killed... a nightmare.<br /> Basically, creating a Ghoul requires just 1 point of Willpower and 1 Vitae ( that the vampire can immediately regain by sucking some of the Ghoul's blood, if he wants ). The Ghoul shortly developes his dot in physical discipline and in 3 days ( enough for a Vinculum ) is ready to be disposed for some suicidal mission.<br /> <br /> <br /> About minimizing risk, that strategy is indeed way safer than constantly hunt for vitae.<br /> <br /> You say that kidnapping humans and bringing them to the basement in the desert to turn them vampires and farm their vitae is risky.<br /> Ok, it is.<br /> <br /> But you really think that kidnapping a human is as risky as hunting a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-19-2015, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T23:10:08-07:00","id":708202,"title":"","content":"In both editions, ghouls aren't considered something made on a whim and expendable. Making a ghoul makes a mortal nearly as powerful as a weak vampire. They are, as Maina said, an investment in time and resources, and one of those resources is something a vampire will always have trouble with, that being people who are both loyal and useful. In addition they're a walking, talking Masquerade breach that can act during hours when a vampire cannot. Consequences for things a ghoul does to shake the Masquerade will land on the regnant.<br /> <br /> You keep describing these games you played, but it sounds like things weren't really 'by the book' to begin with, and based on a lot of Vampire the Masquerade concepts. Which is fine, because it is a toolbox and you can do whatever you want with the game, but when you're asking about how the Vampire the Requiem setting works, you're going to be told how the Vampire the Requiem setting works. I'm guessing you have access to the Ghouls book, looking through it you could see how valued ghouls are. And certainly, many aren't treated well, but they aren't representative of the whole. <a href=\"http://requiemforkingsmouth.wikia.com/wiki/Sun-Walking_Knights\" target=\"_blank\">There's even an entire covenant that revolves around vampires and ghouls being considered equals</a>, with the ghouls enjoying the fruits of their Discipline and Immortality-enhanced labors alongside their Regnants as partners. And all Hunters don't loathe or hate or even want to kill monsters, more than a few of the factions put diplomacy first or are merely attempting to investigate, study, or 'help' monsters.<br /> <br /> Your door problem, for instance. A basic wooden door has a Durability of 1 and a Structure of 5. All you need to damage a door is more than one success. One to beat the Durability, and one to knock the Structure down, as Structure is the equivalent of an object's 'health.' An iron or steel chain would have a Durability of 3 and probably a pretty low Structure, providing you were attempting to break one ring at a time and not burst out of it all like it was an over-inflated balloon. A door might not be broken down in a hurry, but a vampire who has to spend every night in a metal whatever is going to have a long time to work on getting out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-19-2015, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T23:56:16-07:00","id":708299,"title":"","content":"Well, since now I played only with a single troupe so I'm happy to get a different view on the game concept. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T00:55:36-07:00","id":708359,"title":"","content":"The other thing about ghouls in second edition is that when they die there's a small but non-zero chance that they'll get back up again with the ability to process mortal blood into vitae. So now, vampires who take the view that ghouls are disposable tools have a new name: Revenant Factories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T01:12:41-07:00","id":708369,"title":"","content":"And being known for making revenants is not exactly the best way to climb the kindred social ladder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T02:01:47-07:00","id":708421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your door problem, for instance. A basic wooden door has a Durability of 1 and a Structure of 5. All you need to damage a door is more than one success. One to beat the Durability, and one to knock the Structure down, as Structure is the equivalent of an object's 'health.' An iron or steel chain would have a Durability of 3 and probably a pretty low Structure, providing you were attempting to break one ring at a time and not burst out of it all like it was an over-inflated balloon. A door might not be broken down in a hurry, but a vampire who has to spend every night in a metal whatever is going to have a long time to work on getting out. </div> </div> </div>One thing is to damage an object with a well landed blow.<br /> Another thing is to break it applying pressure with zero space to move.<br /> <br /> A strong human can break a chain using an hammer, an axe or a similar implement. But to break that chain simply by pushing would be impossible, and that is exacltly whay a vampire which is tied would need to do. I didn't mean &quot;put on a loose chain with a collar&quot;, like a dog. I meant tied with chains to a rigid structure. He would not have the material space to move his claws enough to strike the chains, so he would have - yes - to burst them all like a ballon.<br /> There was a devotion for elders based on Vigor and Resilience that allowed to do this kind of things, like ripping throug concrete walls bare handed and tearing away chains like paper. Personally, I don't think that getting free from chains is something that a common vampire can do. Tearing them with Claw of the Beast, yes, having space to manouver. But to break free from a think chain, wrists tied together, I would require at least Vigor 4 ( or Vigor 3 and a Strenght of 5 ). One chain. To break four or five chains all together with a steel-support, Vigor 6+ and a specific Devotion.<br /> <br /> <br /> To be more clear, that kind of restrainment:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/deathnote/images/4/4f/Misa_(interrogation).jpg/revision/latest?cb=20120127231958\" target=\"_blank\">http://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/...20120127231958</a><br /> <br /> But with steel bands and the straitjacket made in iron mail.<br /> <br /> And a steel mask with an external crank to open/clos the jaw locker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-19-2015, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T02:08:13-07:00","id":708424,"title":"","content":"I feel like this conversation has gotten off track, has wandered into the wrong alleyway, been ambushed and kidnapped and forced into a rhetoric farm where it's forced to make derails or suffer tortured...metaphors...<br /> <br /> That got away from me. I'm sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 10-19-2015, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T03:47:09-07:00","id":708484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=708421#post708421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing is to damage an object with a well landed blow.<br /> Another thing is to break it applying pressure with zero space to move.<br /> <br /> A strong human can break a chain using an hammer, an axe or a similar implement. But to break that chain simply by pushing would be impossible, and that is exacltly whay a vampire which is tied would need to do. I didn't mean &quot;put on a loose chain with a collar&quot;, like a dog. I meant tied with chains to a rigid structure. He would not have the material space to move his claws enough to strike the chains, so he would have - yes - to burst them all like a ballon.<br /> There was a devotion for elders based on Vigor and Resilience that allowed to do this kind of things, like ripping throug concrete walls bare handed and tearing away chains like paper. Personally, I don't think that getting free from chains is something that a common vampire can do. Tearing them with Claw of the Beast, yes, having space to manouver. But to break free from a think chain, wrists tied together, I would require at least Vigor 4 ( or Vigor 3 and a Strenght of 5 ). One chain. To break four or five chains all together with a steel-support, Vigor 6+ and a specific Devotion.<br /> <br /> <br /> To be more clear, that kind of restrainment:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/deathnote/images/4/4f/Misa_(interrogation).jpg/revision/latest?cb=20120127231958\" target=\"_blank\">http://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/...20120127231958</a><br /> <br /> But with steel bands and the straitjacket made in iron mail.<br /> <br /> And a steel mask with an external crank to open/clos the jaw locker.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And right back to the &quot;perfect implementation&quot; problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T06:56:43-07:00","id":708705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=706990#post706990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Baaldam:<br /> <br /> I don't know if that works in second edition, but in first edition you can leave a vampire with a stick in his heart, and he's fully unconscious and totally helpless. Also, a vampire can be feed ( and therefore produce Vitae that may then be harvested with a syringe ) without even removing the stick. The only moment a vampire would be conscious would be to Embrace a new one, or to be interrogated / tortured, and only one vampire at time. In every other moment they would all be sticked and in torpor.<br /> <br /> These vampire would be both chained and in torpor with a stick in the heart. I don't see many escaping opportunities. Also, they would not requires cells and spaces, nor jailers or guards; just a battery chicken structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually, yes. But staking per se doesn't send a vampire automatically into Torpor, meaning it might be still conscious and capable of using any mental powers. Auspex will be a straight problem only at the highest levels and Dominate is of limited use if one can't speak, but Majesty, Obfuscate, Nightmare and Animalism can disrupt things - and cause atrociously gory deaths, in the last one's case - quite handily to one who underestimates its prey. Also, kindred transform, remember - put them in a weird situation and given enough time &amp; exertion of will, something will change with them, adapting to their problem. It may take years or decades, but i would guess the ghoul has to look out for long run, no?<br /> <br /> It can work for some, for a time, not all of them, all the time. Yes, not having at least some watchers for one's &quot;chicken coop&quot; would definitely be a very bad idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=706990#post706990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also guess that keeping all them less one in torpor would solve Blood Simpathy problem ( I don't think that torpor nightmares spread to awake vampires; if that would the case, all vampires in the world would go mad in short time ).</div> </div> </div> </div>It might diminish the problems in that area indeed, at least in relation to kindred outside the prisioners - an extended slavery &amp; milking scenario with a vampire and its multiple coerced childer could result in recurrent pressure upon the blood ties could form some kind of link or circuit, if such a thing happens torpor might become useless as a measure to contain blood sympathy sendings/communication.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=706990#post706990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is, definetly, the most riskful part of the plan, I agree.<br /> But, one observation: Hunters and fugitive Ghouls take that risk every single time they hunt. The farming Ghoul would need to take it only one time.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but they can simply run away after the hunt, unlike an operation that needs an ever bigger cellar to bury the corpses, beside a lot of other logistic details to deal with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=706990#post706990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vitae becomes normal blood minutes after being harvested. It can't be traded, at least not by transporting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There might be rituals for that - and even without this, it would be a matter of moving one or two staked kindred while arranging one's monthly meeting for vitae trading. Requires some work and a bit more mutual trust, but compare with keeping a dozen, or dozens of kindred, in the way you have described so far.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-19-2015, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T07:11:30-07:00","id":708720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=708705#post708705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> staking per se doesn't send a vampire automatically into Torpor</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate to break it to you but that is <i>precisely</i> what it does in Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T11:22:06-07:00","id":709060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=708720#post708720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate to break it to you but that is <i>precisely</i> what it does in Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, it has <b>been</b> some time since i last read the book... could you reference the page for clarity's sake then, please?<br /> <br /> That said, can a torpid vampire actually process blood into vitae or it all goes straight into healing/waking the corpse?<br /> Because that's another detail to account for, i guess...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T11:28:27-07:00","id":709066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=709060#post709060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, it has <b>been</b> some time since i last read the book... could you reference the page for clarity's sake then, please?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire the Requiem, p177, 'The staked vampire immediately collapses into torpor, appearing stone dead for all that a mortal could tell.'<br /> <br /> Blood and Smoke, p105, 'When a wooden stake penetrates the Kindred heart, the vampire immediately enters torpor. Unlike normal torpor, he awakens immediately upon the stake\u2019s removal, but not before.'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T11:52:33-07:00","id":709116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=709066#post709066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampire the Requiem, p177, 'The staked vampire immediately collapses into torpor, appearing stone dead for all that a mortal could tell.'<br /> <br /> Blood and Smoke, p105, 'When a wooden stake penetrates the Kindred heart, the vampire immediately enters torpor. Unlike normal torpor, he awakens immediately upon the stake\u2019s removal, but not before.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks a bunch, i was thinking of it as colateral to being paralyzed for days or weeks with nothing to feed upon, had completely forgotten the torpor condition was immediate to staking.<br /> <br /> Certainly makes &quot;storage&quot; simpler - problem being, from a &quot;vitae milker&quot; standpoint, if a torpid kindred will actually process forcibly fed or injected blood into vitae while in that state...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T11:56:43-07:00","id":709123,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about that point myself.<br /> <br /> Still, staking is not easy. In first edition you need to make an attack with a -4 dice penalty, and still must inflict at least three points of lethal damage. In second, you attack at a -3 penalty, after factoring Defense, and must inflict five points of damage. That's not counting the various ways vampires have to eliminate that weakness or make it more difficult like wearing armor. A lot of the combat-oriented characters we see in white room simulations can probably do it with ease but it's unlikely my character could pull it off. He'd have an easier time just eating them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-19-2015, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T14:19:40-07:00","id":709299,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure you can feed a torpid kindred. The Ghouls book had a ghoul family that kept their torpid regnant in a bath tub and periodically kidnapped people to feed him with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T15:57:16-07:00","id":709488,"title":"","content":"This discussion is helpful, if only, to stage the big reveal for a game in which the Big Bad has set this operation up. Even if the mechanics are a little suspect, I really want to use this idea for a depraved, high blood potency, elder. I'm imagining a well-funded conspiracy to keep a beloved Priscus fed on kindred blood. Perhaps the player characters have unwittingly aided the conspiracy the whole time. &quot;Oh, there's Steven, that vamp we helped detain for a masquerade breach.&quot; *points to body suspended in a matrix battery.*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Improper use of inverted commas, Hoover!&quot; - Herr Starr","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8536-nutshell","name":"Nutshell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T03:40:49-07:00","id":710305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=709299#post709299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure you can feed a torpid kindred. The Ghouls book had a ghoul family that kept their torpid regnant in a bath tub and periodically kidnapped people to feed him with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there was that one reference, good catch indeed. While i'm not certain it works for waking the torpid (systems overall seem to imply it's vitae, not mortal blood, that jumpstarts that from what i remember), the ghouls own context implies a torpid kindred can still generate vitae in that state, otherwise that ghoul family would be pretty screwed. So staked kindred might indeed be usable as vitae sources to &quot;milk&quot; while being regularly fed, making the whole operation far more manageable to operate as long as one has decent room for storage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T05:03:00-07:00","id":710376,"title":"","content":"Vitae of a vampire 2 points of blood potency higher, IIRC. Which means that at bp 9 or 10 it's <i>impossible</i> to wake one up early that way. <br /> <br /> Although depending on how you interpret it a strix possessing one and then releasing them would do it. Which obviously never happens because why the hell would a strix release a host that powerful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-20-2015, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T05:26:11-07:00","id":710418,"title":"","content":"The Glass Armonium was used in the Nosferatu clanbook to awaken a torpid vampire. Not just any vampire, but Grigor Swancott, the vampire in the tub feasted upon by the Gravenor ghouls. Presumably there are safe ways to do it, if not easy ones.<br /> <br /> It looks as if they didn't just tap him like a keg, they chewed flesh from him. In the VII book there's a ghoul who becomes a vampire by devouring an entire vampire. Maybe since the Vitae is infused in everything, one can't just stick a straw in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-20-2015, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T08:11:24-07:00","id":710592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, staking is not easy. In first edition you need to make an attack with a -4 dice penalty, and still must inflict at least three points of lethal damage. In second, you attack at a -3 penalty, after factoring Defense, and must inflict five points of damage. That's not counting the various ways vampires have to eliminate that weakness or make it more difficult like wearing armor. A lot of the combat-oriented characters we see in white room simulations can probably do it with ease but it's unlikely my character could pull it off. He'd have an easier time just eating them. </div> </div> </div>Trying to stake a vampire in hand-to-hand combat is next to suicidal for a human.<br /> Even an extremely skilled fighter ( strenght or dexterity 3, melee 3 + specialization ) would have only around 3% chance to do 3 points of damage with a single shoot. Not even that against a light armor or a decent Defense.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, a carefully and quietely aimed crossbow shoot from 150 yard on an unaware vampire, right in the back, is reasonably workable.<br /> <br /> ( extreme range: -2, aiming to hearth -4, aiming for 3 rounds +3, binocular aimer and laser punctator + 3, good quality crossbow +2 dices to attack and 3 additional dices to damage if the shoot lands )<br /> <br /> Final modifier: +2 dices to attack, 3 more dices for damage, no Defense allowed. Even a moderately skilled sniper, with some effort ( spending 1 Willpower ) would have high chances of success.<br /> And if he fails, he's far enough for a safe escape.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And right back to the &quot;perfect implementation&quot; problem. </div> </div> </div>Even without knowing precisely what he can do, it would be the bare minimum safety measures I would adopt to deal with a superstrong monster with psychic powers. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-20-2015, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T08:53:22-07:00","id":710672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=710592#post710592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Final modifier: +2 dices to attack, 3 more dices for damage, no Defense allowed. Even a moderately skilled sniper, with some effort ( spending 1 Willpower ) would have high chances of success.<br /> And if he fails, he's far enough for a safe escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your character trying to break down a door had similar odds without using Willpower and you said they didn't manage it. It's the type of thing you can only try once, because you're not going to be able to stand there and aim another three rounds. Celerity would eliminate your chance to escape, but you're of course targeting a vampire without celerity or firearms or ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T09:03:43-07:00","id":710681,"title":"","content":"There's a reason Dracula had Van Helsing stake Drac while the latter was <i>asleep.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T09:08:33-07:00","id":710693,"title":"","content":"Direct threats like fire, sun and collapsing buildings awaken vampires. I have to imagine an impending staking would fit the list. There's still a roll to wake up. Haven is a nice merit for that, gives some bonuses.<br /> <br /> Cheiron, I think, has things planned out, with members of cells each assigned to hold limbs while one stakes, presumably with a ton of bonuses from it. Hopefully they haven't stored their heart in a jar somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T09:19:28-07:00","id":710746,"title":"","content":"That's the thing. They don't notice the stake until it goes in, and against a vamp in daysleep I'd expect a Killing Blow to be viable. So the stake goes in, and the vamp is torpid before they get a chance to wake up. <br /> <br /> <i>Then</i> you can drag them into the sun or set them on fire with no risk of them waking up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T09:22:22-07:00","id":710756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your character trying to break down a door had similar odds without using Willpower and you said they didn't manage it. </div> </div> </div>Let's be more specific. I said I would not allow a HUMAN, mundane character, to break a SOLID ( thick ) wooden door with is bare shoulders or hands, because he would crash his bones and flesh. A robust human with an axe or a pick would be able to fell a door with a good blow or two, so would be a vampire with Feral Claws or Vigor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Celerity would eliminate your chance to escape, but you're of course targeting a vampire without celerity or firearms or ghouls. </div> </div> </div>Celerity enaches speed, but it doesn't allow to cover 150 yards in a couple of rounds. If the sniper is in a van, with the engine on, he has the time to escape. I would use a van because it hides the sniper from potential witnesses, but also a motorbike or a car would do.<br /> <br /> Also, if I shoot someone from 150 yards to the back ( and I would have to wait he's giving me the back, elseway he could notice the red point of the punctator ), how can he understand from where exactly the shoot came from? Crossbows to dot make a *bang* nor they make a flash.<br /> A Meketh with the right Devotion ( Quicken Sight ) mabye would be able to do that. The majority of vampires would not be able to identify the sniper's position on the spot.<br /> <br /> About ghouls ( and mundane bodyguards / servants / thugs ) , that would be a problem.<br /> The safest way would be to search for a lone hunting vampire, probably a Gangrel or a Daeva.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I guess that hunting vampires would be for the most young, or at worst Ancillae. Elders have herds and plenty of blood dolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-20-2015, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T09:36:44-07:00","id":710772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=710756#post710756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would not allow a HUMAN, mundane character, to break a SOLID ( thick ) wooden door with is bare shoulders or hands, because he would crash his bones and flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if they break it, but get a dislocated shoulder or something in return?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T09:41:16-07:00","id":710777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=710746#post710746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the thing. They don't notice the stake until it goes in</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say this? You don't think a hunter standing over you with a hammer and stake is a direct threat?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=710756#post710756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's be more specific. I said I would not allow a HUMAN, mundane character, to break a SOLID ( thick ) wooden door with is bare shoulders or hands, because he would crash his bones and flesh. A robust human with an axe or a pick would be able to fell a door with a good blow or two, so would be a vampire with Feral Claws or Vigor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to when you said, '<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My Meketh blogger / martial artist, despite having Strenght 3 and a dot of Vigor, had an hard time breaking a solid wooden door.' The odds are similar. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Celerity enaches speed, but it doesn't allow to cover 150 yards in a couple of rounds. </div> </div> </div>If the vampire is fantastically Attributed, that's exactly what it does. But an average celerity vampire would take more than a couple of terms, they'd still be able to manage to outrun a mortal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would use a van because it hides the sniper from potential witnesses, but also a motorbike or a car would do. </div> </div> </div>Are you really worrying about witnesses? You just knocked a vampire into torpor, you're going to need to go up to them and do something unless you want to just be an annoyance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if I shoot someone from 150 yards to the back ( and I would have to wait he's giving me the back, elseway he could notice the red point of the punctator ), how can he understand from where exactly the shoot came from? Crossbows to dot make a *bang* nor they make a flash. </div> </div> </div>No, but a bolt flying harmlessly by you is pretty easy to see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The majority of vampires would not be able to identify the sniper's position on the spot. </div> </div> </div>I disagree with that. The bigger issue is that most vampires wouldn't be able to do anything about it, as most vampires don't have Celerity to catch up to you, or Auspex to instantly identify you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T09:49:07-07:00","id":710796,"title":"","content":"Also some crossbows make a fairly loud snapping noise when you fire them. It's not exactly a gunshot, but you might still hear it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T10:06:50-07:00","id":710845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=710777#post710777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but a bolt flying harmlessly by you is pretty easy to see.<br /> <br /> <br /> I disagree with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vietnam veterans would disagree. They had an hell of a time finding vietcong snipers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also some crossbows make a fairly loud snapping noise when you fire them. It's not exactly a gunshot, but you might still hear it. </div> </div> </div>From 150 yards? Even with Auspex, the sound would be covered by the normal noise of a city.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you really worrying about witnesses? You just knocked a vampire into torpor, you're going to need to go up to them and do something unless you want to just be an annoyance. </div> </div> </div>When the vampire is down, getting him on the van would require a minute, but the ambush could last hours. Waiting for the right moment, when the vampire has his back turned and is enough clearly in sight, possibly stopped for a second, would require a lot of patience and during that time being spotted with a gun by a passerby would be a problem. Inside a van you are in the shadows but can see outside, and from 3 sides you're covered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the vampire is fantastically Attributed, that's exactly what it does. But an average celerity vampire would take more than a couple of terms, they'd still be able to manage to outrun a mortal. </div> </div> </div>They can't outride a veichle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, but a bolt flying harmlessly by you is pretty easy to see. </div> </div> </div>You can roughly deduce the direction it came but, unless you are able to clearly see the angle of the shoot, you can't know from where exactly it came. 150 yards are quite a long distance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-20-2015, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T10:12:27-07:00","id":710852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=710845#post710845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vietnam veterans would disagree. They had an hell of a time finding vietcong snipers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bullets aren't bolts. Bullets travel many times faster than crossbow bolts and are much smaller besides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-20-2015, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T10:26:02-07:00","id":710868,"title":"","content":"Well...<br /> hunting vampires is hardly a risk-free activity. No way to know how much strong is the monster.<br /> <br /> But all in all, I think that snipering from a van ready to go is less riskful than jumping on the vampire with a stick and wrestle him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T13:06:30-07:00","id":711147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=710868#post710868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well...<br /> hunting vampires is hardly a risk-free activity. No way to know how much strong is the monster.<br /> <br /> But all in all, I think that snipering from a van ready to go is less riskful than jumping on the vampire with a stick and wrestle him.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But remember how fast vampires can recuperate. Sure, you might be able to snipe them, but can you be so sure you can rush to the vamp's location and detain them before they're back on their feet? There's also the possibility of their supernatural reflexes, enhanced senses and supernatural durability allowing them to detect, dodge or flat out tank the shot. In fact, there's also a devotion that combines Celerity with Auspex to allow the vampire to see in bullet time, which could theoretically locate the bolt's trajectory.<br /> <br /> <br /> And as for not being able to outrun a vehicle? Keep in mind that there is such a thing as speed limits and traffic in cities, and with Celerity, a vampire's running speed can approach just under the triple digits. How are you going to drive a van down a crowded street with a vampire darting through alleyways and roof tops at 60 miles per hour?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-20-2015, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T21:37:47-07:00","id":711754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But remember how fast vampires can recuperate. Sure, you might be able to snipe them, but can you be so sure you can rush to the vamp's location and detain them before they're back on their feet? </div> </div> </div>I would never try to do something so riskful if not forced. If the vampire isn't down and torpid with a quadrel in the hearth, I would immediately flee, leave the city and try somewhere else.<br /> <br /> About the other superpowers, yes, it's the kind of things that a powerful vampire would be able to do. I could object that Celerity and Resilience have to be activated, with Vitae cost, before being hit and are not activated reflexively; so it would require a mid-power and paranoid vampire to be always &quot;battlemode on&quot;. Also, being the average speed of an athletic human around 25 km /h, it would be needed at least Celerity 4 to reach the triple digit.<br /> So, if the target happen to be an expert and paranoid vampire which goes around with his power always activated, that knows the right devotion and have Celerity 4, the would-be sniper is screwed.<br /> <br /> But that would seriously be bad luck.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Little consideration.<br /> In &quot;World of Darkness - Antagonists&quot; I read about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> - Ryan Duffy, web designer and coke/anfetamine addict with HIV ( Constitution 1 ); killed his first vampire with the kitchen knife he used to chop coke, the second one with a gasoline water pistol and a lighter<br /> - William Kidderminister, an overweight drunk night-guard; killed his first vampire pistol-whipping her in the head repeatedly<br /> - Josef Evan, 80 years old bum; kills a vampire shooting him 5 times with a revolver<br /> - Julia Snow, a girl without martial art or military training that managed to kill some vampire by luring them and surprise-hitting with a combat knife<br /> <br /> <br /> So I thought: if untrained people with poor or no pianification somehow managed to take down vampires, a sniper with decent training and a carefully prepared ambush would have high chances of success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-21-2015, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T22:37:15-07:00","id":711830,"title":"","content":"Celerity and Resilience have passive benefits that do not require activation.<br /> <br /> Also there's a contest for surprise, so you might not catch kindred by surprise every time.<br /> <br /> edit: what the heck is &quot;pianification?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T22:49:46-07:00","id":711853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Celerity and Resilience have passive benefits that do not require activation. </div> </div> </div>In first edition NWod, no, they require 1 Vitae expenditure and the benefits lasts for 1 scene. In second edition, I don't know.<br /> If someone is walking on the street and a quadrel bolts flies at him from a long distance, either he have Auspex activated, or he expect to be snipered, or he's caught by surprise.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I italianized the word &quot;planification&quot;. I mean, preparation. To prepare a plan in details, to not do anything improvised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T23:10:13-07:00","id":711881,"title":"","content":"I keep forgetting you're using the obsolete rules.<br /> <br /> They still get a surprise roll, modified as necessary. Esp. if they have Auspex, which in first edition can do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T23:34:01-07:00","id":711892,"title":"","content":"Mh...<br /> well, if the vampire is actively alert to potential dangers - and I guess most of them are - that would be plausible.<br /> <br /> There would be many things to consider. If there is only one veichle in the area, it might draw the attention. Also, if the crossbow have metal parts not covered by plastic or gum, it could reflect light. Actually, from 150 meters it would be hard to notice but not impossible.<br /> A meticulous hunter should wear nothing metallic and cover with black paste the metal parts of the crossbow, take care the van isn't the only veichle in the area and it doesn't look unusual.<br /> <br /> To be more safe, he should put anti-leak tyres and internally reinforce the van with metal plates, expecially the car doors. Cover internally the car windows with several layes of see-through plastic to make harder break them and, if he has enough time and Manuality skill, assemble internal metal shutters. That way the van would look normal from the outside but be able to work as an armored vehicle if needed.<br /> <br /> Also, I would keep a short range weapon at hand, probably a sawn-off shotgun. A double bottom suitcase would be needed to minimize risk to be arrested by a random cop ( if the van is stopped for a routine control on the route for the ambush place ). Also, a double bottom car trunk to hide the torpid vampire, if succesful.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Before you say &quot;that would require perfect knowlege&quot;, I would do these things for every kind of superstrong, superfast, superthough monster I happened to hunt.<br /> It would be &quot;basic monster-hunting protocol&quot;. The only specific knowledge required for the plan is knowing about the stick in the hearth and the torpor.<br /> <br /> If I were out to kill instead of capture, I would do something similar, but I would use an heavy riftle, put myself at a greater distance and aim for the head.<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way...<br /> I wonder if a wooden bullet would do the trick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 10-21-2015, 03:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T04:30:09-07:00","id":712185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=711892#post711892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mh...<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I would keep a short range weapon at hand, probably a sawn-off shotgun. A double bottom suitcase would be needed to minimize risk to be arrested by a random cop ( if the van is stopped for a routine control on the route for the ambush place ). Also, a double bottom car trunk to hide the torpid vampire, if succesful.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Before you say &quot;that would require perfect knowlege&quot;, I would do these things for every kind of superstrong, superfast, superthough monster I happened to hunt.<br /> It would be &quot;basic monster-hunting protocol&quot;. The only specific knowledge required for the plan is knowing about the stick in the hearth and the torpor.<br /> <br /> If I were out to kill instead of capture, I would do something similar, but I would use an heavy riftle, put myself at a greater distance and aim for the head.<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way...<br /> I wonder if a wooden bullet would do the trick.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The only reason a human should be engaging a vampire in close range is as a last resort, so I'm assuming the shotgun is there so you don't have to worry about accuracy.<br /> <br /> On the subject of killing a vampire through pistol whipping, that seems to contradict what I've been lead to believe. It's supposed to be really difficult to kill a vampire through blunt force trauma such as beating them to death. Bashing damage is the easiest to heal from and you pretty much need to pummel somebody to convert it into lethal.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the wooden bullet, I'm going to take a quote from another thread that is specifically focused towards this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/711263-wood-bullets?p=711374#post711374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wooden bullets are actually a real thing... and are generally used like rubber bullets: crowd control. Shooting someone with a wooden bullet can easily hurt them significantly, but they have trouble penetrating skin; let alone muscle and bone. It's theoretically possible to do something like Hod rounds from Hunter, but if you know you're hunting vampires, just use a modern crossbow with wooden shafted bolts; it's a hell of a lot easier, cheaper, and frankly less suspicious (&quot;I fletch my own bolts with wood instead of buying them,&quot; vs. &quot;I'm using firearms ammunition that is harder to detect with metal detectors... to hunt vampires, not to try to skate around security!&quot;)).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I've noticed we seem to be pointing out all the things that could possibly go wrong with this plan. While it's true there are many ways this could screw up, we're assuming that the vampire he's going after has the ability to do all of these things, instead of only some or even none at all. Plus, I just realized the plan is intended for a Ghoul, which means he does have some abilities of his own to throw out, just not on the same level as a proper vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-21-2015, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T05:09:34-07:00","id":712228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only reason a human should be engaging a vampire in close range is as a last resort, so I'm assuming the shotgun is there so you don't have to worry about accuracy. </div> </div> </div>Yep, it's a last resort weapon is the main plan ( snipering ) goes really wrong for some reason. It does not require much accuracy and buckshots can render flesh much better than bullets.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T05:12:29-07:00","id":712231,"title":"","content":"Pretty much <i>everything </i>does bashing to vampires in second edition, so pistol whipping is no more or less effective than stabbing or shooting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T05:51:26-07:00","id":712288,"title":"","content":"@Elfive Only kind of. Automatic damage still matters for weapons, and I can't imagine pistol whipping being more than +0 damage. Guns and knives may also do bashing, but guns will add bonus damage, and so will stabby things larger than a knife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T05:56:31-07:00","id":712291,"title":"","content":"Well, I think using a gun as a club probably falls under improvised weapon, so it really depends on how durable the gun is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T07:43:33-07:00","id":712390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=710418#post710418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Glass Armonium was used in the Nosferatu clanbook to awaken a torpid vampire. Not just any vampire, but Grigor Swancott, the vampire in the tub feasted upon by the Gravenor ghouls. Presumably there are safe ways to do it, if not easy ones.<br /> <br /> It looks as if they didn't just tap him like a keg, they chewed flesh from him. In the VII book there's a ghoul who becomes a vampire by devouring an entire vampire. Maybe since the Vitae is infused in everything, one can't just stick a straw in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know about those bits, specially considering my main grievance against the &quot;inject blood, convert to vitae&quot; methodology was its lack of the essential element that is feeding, the actual predatory/cannibal act of consuming another. Consuming bits of the vampire along with the blood to actually extact vitae sounds much better and ressonant in that aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T08:06:29-07:00","id":712429,"title":"","content":"I don't think they injected it. I think they'd slit the victim's throat over his mouth. A funnel may have been involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T10:16:28-07:00","id":712627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=712288#post712288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Elfive ] I can't imagine pistol whipping being more than +0 damage. Guns and knives may also do bashing, but guns will add bonus damage, and so will stabby things larger than a knife.</div> </div> </div> </div>As luck would have it, I recently discussed pistol whipping with someone who I consider to have... <i>reliable experience</i>, in that regard. He's pretty enthusiastically of the opinion that a gun barrel is in the &quot;small club&quot; category, being smaller, but heavier. So, +1 tops, yeah.<br /> <br /> [/nitpick]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T18:18:26-07:00","id":716578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/704348-it-s-possible-to-coerce-a-vampire-to-embrace-someone?p=712429#post712429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they injected it. I think they'd slit the victim's throat over his mouth. A funnel may have been involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant on the OP's concept actually. Really not seeing the Gravenors doing things in such a clean &amp; sanitary way either. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}